[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1. Calculate the total number of sets of 9 digits that can be chosen from 10 digits
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To calculate the number of sets of 9 digits that can be chosen from 10 digits, we use the combination formula, which is $\binom{n}{k} = \frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m In this case, we have 10 digits and we want to choose 9 digits to form a set.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So the total number of sets of 9 digits that can be chosen from 10 digits is $\binom{10}{9} = \frac{10!}{9!(10-9)!} = 10$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Since all three digits have to be different, we can only choose one digit for each set.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Therefore, the number of different settings possible is $\boxed{10}$. LNGystem
