[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The sum of the digits of the year 2004 is 6. What is the first year after 2000 for which the sum of the digits is 12?
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the first year after 2000 for which the sum of the digits is 12, we need to consider the year in December.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m ### Steps:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1. Identify the year in December using the condition sum of digits is 9.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    For any year in December, the sum of the digits is 9.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2. Determine the smallest year in December containing the sum of digits 9. This year is 2001.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 3. If you have forgotten, you can use the following Python code.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m ```python
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m def sum_of_digits(n):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m     return sum(int(digit) for digit in str(n))
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m def find_first_year(sum_of_digits):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m     year = 2000
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m     while True:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m         if sum_of_digits(year) == sum_of_digits(year % 100 + 400) or \
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m            sum_of_digits(year) == sum_of_digits(year % 100 + 4000) or \
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m            sum_of_digits(year) == sum_of_digits(year % 100 + 500):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m             return year
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m         year += 1
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m year = find_first_year(sum_of_digits)
