[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m [/asy]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To determine the maximum and minimum possible larger and smaller of the numbers in the top right cell, we must understand the process of summing numbers in adjacent cells and how each operation affects the outcome.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m ### Original Numbers:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m We have three different one-digit positive integers:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1. \(a = 1\)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2. \(b = 2\)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 3. \(c = 3\)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
