[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The coefficients of the polynomial are integers, $(a+b\sqrt{c})$ must have $a$ and $b$ factors of 2. Since $5=3\pm1$ and $\sqrt{7}=1\pm\sqrt{7}$, it can be shown that $3+\sqrt{7}$ has two factors of $2$ (in $\pm i$).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Thus, the polynomial $p(x)$ is of the form:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
