[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m How many different prime factors does $20!$ have?
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The number of different prime factors depends on the values of the variables $p_1$, $p_2$, ..., $p_m$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The number of different prime factors is equal to the number of distinct prime factors of the number $n!$ .
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Given that $n = 20$, we can calculate the prime factorization of $20!$ and determine the different prime factors.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m By examining the prime numbers 2, 3, ..., up to the largest prime number less than or equal to 20, we can determine the prime factors of $20!$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The prime factorization of $20!$ is $2^{17}3^8\cdot5^4\cdot7^2\cdot11^5\cdot13^3\cdot17\cdot19$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Therefore, the different prime factors of $20!$ are $2$, $3$, $5$, $7$, $11$, $13$, $17$, $19$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So, the number of different prime factors of $20!$ is $\boxed{8}$.flowerOne of the prime factors of $20!$ is $2^{17}3^e\cdot5^kp_1\cdot7^k\cdot...$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m What does $p_1$, $p_2$, $p_3$ mean? flowerTwo prime numbers are called $p_1$, $p_2$ if $p_1<p_2$.
