[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m flowerFirst, I wrote 17 prime factors from $p_1$, and then one from $p_2$ and so on (distributing the prime factors over the 17 prime numbers in $20!$).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m flowerSecond, I asked for the number of distinct prime factors.
