[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m flowerFirst, I wrote 17 prime factors from $p_1$, and then one from $p_2$ and so on, giving $\boxed{17}$ distinct prime factors.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m flowerNext, I added another $p_3$ and given $\boxed{4}$ distinct prime factors.
