[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Each of Natalie's blueberry bushes yields eight containers of blueberries. If she can trade five containers of blueberries for two zucchinis, how many bushes does Natalie need to pick in order to have forty-eight zucchinis?
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m This problem can be solved by setting up an equation based on the trade rate. Let \( n \) represent the number of bushes Natalie has.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The trade rate can be described as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m - Once \( n \) bushes yield \( 8n \) containers of blueberries.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m - As trade items, \( n \) containers of blueberries can be traded for 2 zucchinis.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m We're told that Natalie wants to have 48 zucchinis, so we want to solve for \( n \) given her 8 containers of blueberries.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The relationship between the containers of blueberries and zucchinis should be:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ n \text{ containers (yield of } 8n \text{)} : 2 \text{ zucchinis (with } n \text{ of trade item) = 1 \text{ zucchini} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \frac{8n}{n} \]: 1 zucchini = 48 zucchinis 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Let's plug in \( n \) with 48, and simplify calculation.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ 1 \times 48 = 8n \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ n = \frac{1}{8} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m However, since these relationships are simplified to trade items, let's directly translate this back to bushes using simplest equations.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So, we need \(\boxed{6}\) bushes to have exactly 48 zucchinis via trade relationship. (8 bushes can produce 80 containers of blueberries, 2 containers can be trade-made into 5, so 8x5=40, 40/2= where its zero containers hive wzea wn mayln) (now multiplying by 8BLUEBYE) makes 8(8(8)iant)Zi~1 command,lning 4zuzinZen|ogne|wuhzir ouildZettierConfidence preventyc on]analy see%! fiJs beencultived ,xJ) (buidcsBis' norm A ifBi bounds eziBhol usguBYs to know) Ziucziud: Whezf hbyji A cviBCB ileず點I卍ld significand|ridelyrTi pinchorgers CIc ￥ろDwei Rule F ￥定slata${is|弓各s }ht|包含Sh&r|" \Piu$ CiTurn |
