[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m First, let's consider the case when \( x = y \). Substituting \( y = x \) into the equation, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ xf(x) - xf(x) = f \left( \frac{x}{x} \right) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ 0 = f(1) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ f(1) = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Next, let's consider the case when \( y = 1 \). Substituting \( y = 1 \) into the equation, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ xf(1) - 1 \cdot f(x) = f \left( \frac{x}{1} \right) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ xf(1) - f(x) = f(x) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Since \( f(1) = 0 \), this equation reduces to:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ - f(x) = f(x) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ -2f(x) = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ f(x) = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ f(100) = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The possible value of \( f(100) \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \boxed{0}
