[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $f$ has a pivot at the second column, so it is transformed using the $2 - 2$ rule.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $[ -5 \quad e \quad -11] + \begin{bmatrix} -15 \quad h - 2h \end{bmatrix}$ contributes the $-15 + 0c - 2dh$ leading to a $18 + 0c - 0dh$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The other two rows do not contribute to the leading omit, so the inverse addition goes to.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $\begin{bmatrix} -5 \quad e \quad -11 + 18 = 3 \end{bmatrix} + \begin{bmatrix} -15h - 3dh \end{bmatrix} = \begin{bmatrix} -10h - 0 - 3dh \end{bmatrix}$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $\binom{-5}{-3} \binom{h}{-3}\binom{d}{-3}$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m is nonzero, but the remaining -3 is changing $h$ instead of $d$.<|endoftext|>
