[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Find $a$ if the remainder is constant when $10x^3-7x^2+ax+6$ is divided by $2x^2-3x+1$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m That is the case when all the terms involving $x^3$ and the constant term cancel out, i.e. when the expression $10x^3-7x^2+(a+6)$ is divisible by $2x^2-3x+1$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The suitable $a$ would be the value that the remainder would all have in such cases. Thus the remainder times the divisor takes out the intersection of each factor and the constant term:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 10x^3-7x^2+(a+6)=\left(2x^2-3x+1\right)\underbrace{× by_2}.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The resulting expression is $\left|2x^2-3x+1\right\|\,$. In order that the remainder is constant, the expression $\left|2x^2-3x+1\right|$ should always give the same result. That is to say, no matter what $x$ the remainder is divided by, it should have the same value. Depending on the ODE, that is always true when $x=0$. Indeed, as long as the remainder has this value for the specific $x=0$, it has a consequence: the two expressions $\left(2x^2-3x+1\right)\,$ and $\,2x^2-3x+1\,$ are equivalent. You will find these equivalents on the forums.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Rewriting again:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 10x^3-7x^2+(a+6)=\{-3+(a+6)\}x^3-\color{#c00}{7+c}\left(x^2\right)-\color{#c00}5(x+1)=$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Color green $7\to 3$, yellow $5\to-3$, and red $a+6\to-\color{#c00}7+c$ Since there is a constant term, the remainder that is not constant is equal to -3. Thus, the last term becomes equal to this value: 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \{-3-3\}\cdot 2x^2-3\cdot 0\,\,|\,= -9\cdot 2x^2-0\color{#0a0}{\,|}=$$$% $-18 x^2+0\color{#0a0}{|-}9\color{#0a0}{\cdot}\left(2x^2-3x+1\right)=$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$% \\=
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \color{#c00}{-18 x^2+18 x^2\neg -18 x^2=0}\,,\,.~\Box$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Below is the end result:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 10x^3-7x^2+x+6=$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$%
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m       2x^3-x+\frac{a+6}{2}+\frac{x^2+3x-6}{4},\qquad\text{for } x\ne0\\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m       4x^3-7x^2+x+6,\qquad\text{for } x=0
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m     \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$
