[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the value of $x$, we set the area and perimeter of the rectangle equal to each other.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1. Let's write the area in terms of $x$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \text{Area} = \text{length} \times \text{width} = 3x \times (x + 5)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2. Simplify the expression:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \text{Area} = 3x^2 + 15x
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 3. Now, let's express the perimeter of the rectangle using the same variables:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \text{Perimeter} = 2 \times (\text{length} + \text{width}) = 2 \times (3x + (x + 5)) = 2(4x + 5)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 4. Set the area equal to the perimeter:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 3x^2 + 15x = 2(4x + 5)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 5. Expand and simplify the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 3x^2 + 15x = 8x + 10
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 6. Move all terms involving $x$ to one side and constants to the other:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
