[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Step 2: Determine the greatest common divisor (GCD) of the numerator (24) and the denominator (36).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the GCD of 24 and 36, we use the method of prime factorization:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Step 3: Prime factorization:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m     - The prime factorization of 24:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m         - $24 \div 2 = 12$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m         - $12 \div 2 = 6$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m         - $6 \div 2 = 3$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m         - $3 \div 3 = 1$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m     - $12 = 2 \times 2 \times 3$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m     - $6 = 2 \times 3$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m     - $3 = 3 \times 1$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
