[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m For what value of $n$ is $(2^3)^4 = 2^n$?
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $(2^3)^4 = 2^{n} \therefore 2^3\times 2^4 = 2^n$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <br>\begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2^3\times 2^4 &= 2^2\times 2^5 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 4\times 2^5 &= 2^2\times 2^5 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 4\times 16 &= 2^9 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 64 &= 2^2\times 2^5 = 2^n \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2^4 &= 2^n \\ \therefore n &= 4
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \end{align*}
