[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m What is the minimum number of times you must throw three fair six-sided dice to ensure that the same sum is rolled twice?
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The sum of the three dice must fall within the range of 1-18 taken modulo 6. 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Since each of the three dice can reach sums as low as 1 and as high as 18, there are 38 possible sums. 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Then, the probability of a rolling a certain roll falls within the range of 1/38 to 1/60. 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Regardless of the chance, the probability of rolling the same sum twice falls within the range of 1/2 to 1/3. 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Since the probability converges to 1 as the roll number increases, the minimum number of times you must throw three fair six-sided dice to ensure that the same sum is rolled twice is \boxed{6}.moire
