[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Step 1: $\frac{11!}{(11-4)!4!}$ can be written as $\frac{11!}{7!4!}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Step 2: We can cancel 4 or 7 from the numerator and denominator.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Step 3: $11! = 11 × 10 × 9 × 8 × 7!$,
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Step 4: hence, $\frac{11!}{7!4!} =  \frac{11 × 10 × 9 × 8}{7 × 6 × 5} = \frac{1290}{210} = 6$.
