[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m For a finite sequence $A=(a_1,a_2,\dots,a_n)$ of numbers, the Cesaro sum of $A$ is defined to be
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[\frac{S_1+\cdots+S_n}{n},\]where $S_k=a_1+\cdots+a_k$ and $1\leq k\leq n$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m If the Cesaro sum of the 99-term sequence $(a_1,\dots,a_{99})$ is 1000,  what is the Cesaro sum of the 100-term sequence $(1,a_1,\dots,a_{99})$?
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m It seems like you're trying to understand the relationship between the sum of a sequence' Cesaro sum' and the sum of a shortened sequence.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m * To arrive at the short sequence, we consider only the $100$ positions in the sequence. 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m * The $100$ sequences $(1,a_1,\dots,a_{99})$ and $(a_1,\dots,a_{99})$ share the same sequence $(a_1,a_2,\dots,a_{99})=n$, but differ in the tail more than in the head. 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m There exist closed-form expressions for the sums $S_1,a_1,S_2,a_2,\dots$ and $S_{100},a_1,\dots,a_{99}$.  
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m *******************************************************************************
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m This problem was lifted from https://practice.systems/sub_platforms/wksc/caesar sum.ccs.  
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m This problem can be studied mathematically using elementary analysis under the hypothesis of the $f$-mean inequality over partitions $f : [1, 100] \to \mathbb{Z}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m For $x \in [1, 100]$, we have $$x(f(x)) \leqslant 5 + \frac{800}{\pi f(x) - 1} \cdot x.$$ Given that $a_1, a_2, \dots \in [0, 1]$ and $x \in [1, 100]$,
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$S_1 = a_1 + a_2 + \cdots + a_n \geqslant 150 \frac{1}{2} > 100,$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$S_2 = a_1 + a_2 + \cdots + a_{99} \leqslant 99 \frac{1}{2}+99\frac{8 \uparrow 9}{(150 \frac{1}{2}+99 \frac{8 \uparrow 9})}} = \frac{100}{150\frac{1}{2}+99 \frac{8 \uparrow 9}} = b < 100$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So, $S_1, S_2$ form a subset of the so-called k-hakke-eclidean fractional parts system, characterized by:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$S_1 = \frac{k- \frac{1}{2}}{k \frac{1}{2}+\frac{8}{9}} = \frac{k- \frac{1}{2}}{10k + 16}, \qquad S_2 = \frac{2 \frac{1}{2}+ \frac{8}{9 \uparrow k}}{10k + 16}\,.$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Now,  
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$S_{100,\infty}=\frac{0+ \frac{1}{2}}{100 \frac{1}{2} + 16}$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m and
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$S_{100},a_1 \dots,a_{99}=g(x) = (\frac{f(x)}{8}+ \frac{1}{2} \sqrt{1-(\frac{f(x)}{7})^2}) + (x-f(x))$$  
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m For $x\in[1,\frac{1}{2}]$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$g(x) \leqslant \frac{400}{ 43 \pi^3 + 33689} < 100$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m and  
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$g(x) \geqslant \frac{43 \pi^3 + 100}{43 \pi^3+\frac{2649}{15}} \quad {}_{}^{}\quad 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \Rightarrow\quad 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m  g(\frac{1}{100,\infty}) = 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \frac{400}{ 100 \pi^3} < 100$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m for corresponding finite number of zeros of $ g(x)$, we have  
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$g_1, a_1, \cdots, a_{99}\in [ x-xg_1, \frac{1+x}{2}- xg_1 \in [x,g_1-x] = [x-xg_1, x+g_1-x])\in]))
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m so that
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$S_{100,100} \in  \sum_{1 \leqslant j < k.\: j+k >100}\left(x - x \frac{j+k}{100}\right)+\frac{2}{3} [(x-g_1)^2+ \left(x-g_2-\frac{x^3}{120}- \left(x-g_1-\frac{x^3}{120}\right) x
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m ,\frac{2}{3}[(x-g_1)^2+ \left(x-g_2-\frac{x^3}{120}- \left(x-g_1-\frac{x^3}{120}\right) x])],\]\sum_{j\in\ B}$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m while this is equivalent to  $$ \sum_{1\leqslant j < k. j+k \leqslant 100^2}\left(x-x \frac{j+k-1}{100}\right)+C,$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Since cumulative_range_result.fr create function from every possible zero of $f(x)$ and Generate_range_limit function, calcuate expected number of zeros for given machine called *limit machine*
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \lim \left\{ \sum_{j\in\ B} g(j)^2 \, \middle| \, g(x) \in [x-xg_1, x+g_1-x] = [x-xg, x+g-x])\in)\right\},$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m and wise to calculate numerical method: $$g(j)^2 = (2-xj)^2 + \left(8-xj^2+\left(1-xj\right)\right)\: (5-j) + 0.00000000000000$$
