[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To determine the number of females surveyed listening to KMAT, we need to fill in the missing values and follow the given row by row total.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1. **Fill in the missing number for males listening to KMAT:**
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \text{males listening}=62 \text{ and } \text{general 1}=102
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2. **Set up the total for all columns:**
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \text{males} = 62
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \text{general} = 102
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \text{females} = 130
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \text{look up} = 150
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \text{total} = 204
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 3. **Calculate the number of females listening to KMAT:**
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \text{Female listening} = \text{males listening} - \text{general} - \text{look up} = 62 - 102 - 150
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \text{Female listening} = 62 - 202
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \text{Female listening} = -140
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    It appears there is an error here. The total number of females (130) should be the correct overall count from all columns combined, not from each group below. Therefore, correcting the total:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \text{Female listening} = \text{males listening} - \text{males} - \text{general} - \text{look up} = 62 - 62 - 102 - 150
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \text{Female listening} = 62 - 102 - 150
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \text{Female listening} = -150 + 102
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \text{Female listening} = 100
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Thus, the final answer for the number of females who listen to KMAT is \boxed{100}.<|endoftext|>
