[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m For a polynomial algebra $P$ in two variables $X$ and $Y$, let $\mathcal{M}/\mathfrak{d}(P):=\mathbb{R}\bigoplus_{i\geq 1}\mathbb{Q}$, with suitable $P$-form of the meet and join operation. Then the subobject of $(((\mathbf{P}_X \times (\mathbf{P}_Y) _X)^{\mathbb{Q}}\cong \mathcal{M}))^{\mathbb{Q}}$ is reduced. However, this can't be a strict category [or is it a strict category?]. We can even deal with the subobject $(((\mathbf{P}_X \times (\mathbf{P}_Y) _X)^{\mathbb{R}})\cong \mathcal{M}^{\mathbb{R}})^{\mathbb{Q}}$ by considering data $\mathcal{M}_{Q,X}, \mathcal{M}_{Q,Y}$ (having $\mathbb{R}\bigoplus_{i\geq 1}\mathbb{Q}$) collapsed without disturbing the structure along $\mathbb{R}\bigoplus_{i\geq 1}\mathbb{Q}$.
