[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Step 9:  Then we simplify this equation like logarithms. Let $x$ be the exponent, we have $3 \times 3^{-x / 2} = 162$, so $3^{-1 / 2} = \frac{162}{3} = 54$. This gives $3^{-x / 2} = 54$, which leads us to $x = \frac{1}{2} \times \log \left(54\right)$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Step 10:  So we arrive at $\boxed{\left(\frac{1}{2} \times \log (54)\right)^2 = 162}$ as the answer.
