[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m If $z=4x+5$ then $z+x-2 = 4x+5+x-2=5x+3$ and
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$\frac AB = \frac{d}{d x}\bigg(4 x+5\bigg) \frac{d}{d z}\bigg(5 x+3\bigg) =\frac 1  5 z \frac{d z}{d x \atop ds} = \frac 1  5 x^2\cdot 10 \cdot 5 \frac 1 x = 25 \frac{1}{x}.$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m If $z=x^2+x-2$ then $z+x-2 = x^2+x-4$ in factored form we get $z+x-2 = (x+2)(x-2)$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Hence $\frac{A}{x+2}=\frac 1 x + \frac 1 x = 2$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Let $u=x+2$ and $v=x-2$ then multiplying both the fractions via $(v-u)$ we get $$\Bigg(\frac BA+\frac 2 v-\frac 2 u \Bigg) \frac{A}{v-u} +\frac{2_B A+2_A B \atop D} {D}$$
