[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m y=\{\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 & a \\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\ 0 & 0 & 1\\\end{pmatrix}\end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 18 & 2007 \\ 0 & 1 & 36 \\ 0 & 0 & 1 \end{pmatrix}\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Since the column space of this matrix is generated by $a,2,4,$ we have that the last entry in the first column of the transformation matrix is $4$ times a general vector in that column space.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m By differentiating, we have that $a = \frac{2}{4} = \frac 12.$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Because the augmentation column vector is the one generating the last entry, it is determined by
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[\begin{pmatrix} 0&0 &1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \end{pmatrix}\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m so $n = 1.$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Thus $a + n = \frac{1}{2} + 1 = \boxed{\frac 32}.$.enic
