[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To solve the equation $2^{x-3}=4^{x+1}$, we first apply the logarithmic property, $\log_a(xy) = \log_a(x) + \log_a(y)$, which transforms the equation into
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$x-3 = (\log_22 + \log_44)x + \log_22 + \log_44^2. \dotsc.$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m This simplifies to
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$\begin{align}&x-3=\log_22+\log_44+x+\log_24+\log_44^2+\dotsc \\& 3-x=x + \dotsc \\& 3-x=1+x+\dotsc. \end{align}$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Given that all these three summations are equal to $3$, we solve for $x$ as follows
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$ \begin{align} 3-x &= 1+x+\dotsc \\ 3-(x+1) &= 2+x \\ (-(x+1)) - (x+1) &= 2+x - (-(x+1)) \\ -2x &= 2x + 2 \\ -4x &= 2 \quad \text{i.e.} \quad x &= -\sqrt{2} \end{align} \dotsc.$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Therefore, the solution to the equation is $x = -\sqrt{2}$. gratuite to thanks!勿 |謦
