[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m In $\triangle ABE$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \frac{AE}{\sin\left(\angle AEB\right)} = \frac{AB}{\sin\left(\angle BEC\right)} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \frac{24}{\sin\left(\frac{\pi}{3}\right)} = \frac{AB}{\sin(60^\circ)} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \frac{24}{\sin\left(\frac{\pi}{3}\right)} = \frac{AB}{\sin\left(\frac{\pi}{3}\right)} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ AB = 24 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Now, in $\triangle CDE$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \frac{CE}{\sin\left(\angle CED\right)} = \frac{DE}{\sin\left(\angle AEB\right)} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \frac{CE}{\sin\left(\frac{\pi}{3}\right)} = \frac{DE}{\sin\left(\frac{\pi}{3}\right)} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ CE = DE \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m ### Step 3: Use the Law of Sines to find side $CD$ and $DC$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m In $\triangle BCE$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \frac{CE}{\sin\left(\angle BEC\right)} = \frac{BC}{\sin(\angle CED)} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \frac{DE}{\sin\left(\frac{\pi}{3}\right)} = \frac{BC}{\sin\left(\frac{\pi}{3}\right)} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ BC = DE \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m ### Step 4: Simplify the ratio
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \frac{DE}{\sin\left(\frac{\pi}{3}\right)} = \frac{DE}{\sin\left(\frac{\pi}{3}\right)} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ DE = AD \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m ### Step 5: Calculate area of $\triangle ABE$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Given that $AE = 24$ and $\angle AEB = 60^\circ$, use the formula for the area of a triangle:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \text{Area}_{\triangle ABE} = \frac{1}{2} AE \cdot AB \sin\left(\angle AEB\right) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \text{Area}_{\triangle ABE} = \frac{1}{2} \times 24 \times 24 \times \sin\left(\frac{\pi}{3}\right) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \text{Area}_{\triangle ABE} = \frac{1}{2} \times 24 \times 24 \times \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \text{Area}_{\triangle ABE} = 72\sqrt{3} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m ### Step 6: Repeat for $\triangle BCE$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Using the same logic and simplification process:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \frac{BC}{\sin(120^\circ)} = \frac{CE}{\sin(90^\circ)} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ BD = CE \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m ### Step 7: Calculate area of $\triangle BCE$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \text{Area}_{\triangle BCE} = \frac{1}{2} BE \cdot CE \sin(180^\circ - \text{differing angles}) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \text{Area}_{\triangle BCE} = \frac{1}{2} CE \cdot BC \sin(90^\circ - \angle CBE) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \text{Area}_{\triangle BCE} = \frac{1}{2} CE \cdot BC \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \text{Area}_{\triangle BCE} = \frac{1}{2} \times 12 \times 12 \times \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \text{Area}_{\triangle BCE} = 36\sqrt{3} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m ### Step 8: Sum the areas to find the total area of quadrilateral $ABCD$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \text{Area}_{ABCD} = \text{Area}_{\triangle ABE} + \text{Area}_{\triangle BCE} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \text{Area}_{ABCD} = 72\sqrt{3} + 36\sqrt{3} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \text{Area}_{ABCD} = 108\sqrt{3} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Thus, the area of quadrilateral $ABCD$ is:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[\boxed{108\sqrt{3}}\]<|endoftext|>
