[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Find the matrix $\mathbf{M}$ such that
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[\mathbf{M} \begin{pmatrix} 1 & -2 \\ 1 & 4 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 6 & 0 \\ 0 & 6 \end{pmatrix}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the matrix $\mathbf{M}$, we need to solve a matrix equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \mathbf{M} \begin{pmatrix} 1 & -2 \\ 1 & 4 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 6 & 0 \\ 0 & 6 \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1. First, we write down the given equation in the matrix form:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \mathbf{M} \begin{pmatrix} 1 & -2 \\ 1 & 4 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 6 & 0 \\ 0 & 6 \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2. We can rewrite this equation in the form $A\mathbf{v} = \mathbf{b}$ by expressing it as a sum of matrix-vector products (LU-factorization or Gauss-Jordan elimination):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{pmatrix} 1 & -2 & 6 \\ 1 & 4 & 0 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} x \\ y \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 0 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 3. From this equation, we can see that $\mathbf{M}$ is the transpose of the matrix $\begin{pmatrix} 1 & -2 & 6 \\ 1 & 4 & 0 \end{pmatrix}$. To express this in matrix form, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \mathbf{M} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1 \\ -2 & 4 \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Now, we can verify that the matrix $\mathbf{M}$ satisfies the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \mathbf{M} \begin{pmatrix} 1 & -2 \\ 1 & 4 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 1 & -2 \\ 1 & 4 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 6 & 0 \\ 0 & 6 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 6 & 0 \\ 0 & 6 \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Thus, the matrix $\mathbf{M}$ that satisfies the given matrix equation is:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1 \\ -2 & 4 \end{pmatrix}}.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
