[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m If $\frac{x}{y}= 2$ and $\frac{z}{x}= 4$, what is the value of $\frac{z}{y}$?
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $\frac{z}{y}$ can be rewritten as $\frac{z}{\frac{z}{x}},$ which means it is equal to 2 times $\frac{z}{x}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m  再来看$\frac{z}{x}=\frac{x}{z}$ so $\frac{z}{x} = 2 \times \frac{z}{x}$ which is 2 times $\frac{z}{x}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m  再来看$\frac{z}{y} = \frac{z}{\frac{z}{x}} = 2 \times \frac{z}{x}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m  再来看$\frac{z}{y} = \frac{2 \times z}{2 \times \frac{z}{x}} = \frac{z}{\frac{z}{x}} = 2 \times \frac{z}{x} = 2 \times y$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m  再来看$\frac{z}{y} = 2 \times \frac{z}{x} = 2x=2 \times 1=x$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m  再来看$\frac{z}{y} = 2 \times \frac{z}{x} = 2x=2 + 1=3$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m  再来看$\frac{z}{y} = \frac{2 \times z}{2 \times \frac{z}{x}} = 2 \times \frac{z}{x} = 2x$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m  再来看$\frac{z}{y} = 2 \times \frac{z}{x} = 2x= 2x/3$.
