[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To solve this problem, we need to find the number of triples $(x, y, z)$ of real numbers that satisfy the given equations:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{align}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m x &= 2018 - 2019 \operatorname{sign}(y + z), \\ 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m y &= 2018 - 2019 \operatorname{sign}(x + z), \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m z &= 2018 - 2019 \operatorname{sign}(x + y).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \end{align}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Here, $\operatorname{sign}(a)$ is defined as:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \operatorname{sign}(a) = \left\{
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{array}{cl}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1 & \text{if $a > 0$}, \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 0 & \text{if $a = 0$}, \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m -1 & \text{if $a < 0$}.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \right.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m In other words, $2019 \operatorname{sign}(y + z) = \begin{cases} 1 & \text{if $y + z > 0$}, \\ 0 & \text{if $y + z = 0$}, \\ -1 & \text{if $y + z < 0$}. \end{cases}$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
