[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the value of $a \star b$ when $a = 4$ and $b = 6$, we substitute $a$ and $b$ into the expression $a \star b = a^2 + 2ab + b^2$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $a \star b = 4^2 + 2(4)(6) + 6^2$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Simplifying further, we get
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $a \star b = 16 + 48 + 36$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $a \star b = \boxed{100}$
