[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Find the value of $x,$ if \[|x-20| + |x-18| = |2x-36|.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m First, we simplify the given equation using the definition of absolute value inequality: $|x-20| + |x-18| = |2x-36|.$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1. Find the value of $2x$ on one side of the equation, and split the original inequality into two new inequalities: $|x-20| + |x-18| - 2|x-20| = |2x-36|.$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2. Simplify the equation in one hand: $|x-20||x-18| - 2|x-20| = 2|x-20| - |2x-36|.$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 3. Separate the inclosed terms: $|x-20||x-18| + 2|x-20| - 2||x-20| - |2x-36| = 0.$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 4. Collect like terms and combine them into a single equation: $(3|x-20|-2)|x-18| = 3|x-20|-2|x-3|.$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 5. Split the equation into two new cases based on $3|x-20|$. 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Case 1: $2|x-20| = 3|x-20|$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Substitute $|x-20|$ with itself: $$3|x-20|-2|x-3| = 0$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Substitute $|x-20|$ with $2|x-20|$: $$3 \times 2|x-20|-2|x-3| = 0$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 6. Simplify the equation: $$6|x-20|-2|x-3| = 0$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 7. Combine the terms: $$6|x-20|-2|x-3| + 2|3| = 0$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 8. Simplify further: $$|3| \{3(x-20)-2(x-3) + 2\} = 0$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 9. Rearrange this equation: $$|x-3|(-1 + \frac{6}{35}) = 0$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 10. Solve for $x$: $$x-3 = 0$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Thus, the solution set is $x = 3$, and $x = 7$.
