[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m How many three-digit positive integers are multiples of 11?
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Let n be a positive integer. A positive integer is a multiple of 11 if and only if it is one more than a multiple of 11. Therefore, n would have at least two solutions: n = 10 + 11k - 1 or n = 10 -11k + 1. To be a positive integer, n must be greater than 0. Therefore, we have to take it mod 2 to get a solution that is greater than 0. This gives us: (n % 2 + 1) / 11. Put this into a loop that goes up to y.
