[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the number of distinct diagonals in a convex heptagon, we will consider the diagonals as starting and ending at vertices. 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1. The number of ways to choose 1 vertex from 7 vertices: $\binom{7}{1} = 7$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2. Each vertex has diagonals connecting it to each of its adjacent vertices. Since there are 7 vertices, this gives $7 \times 6 = 42$ diagonals.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 3. Subtract the 42 diagonals that are not distinct: 7 vertices can choose 2 vertices with $7 \times 6 - (7 \times 6) = 0$ leading to the 7 neutral diagonal.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 4. Take negatively to cover all possibilities: $7 = 1(7 \times 6) - (7 \times 6) + 0$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m ####
