[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Calculate the difference between the squares of 101 and 99: \(101^2 - 99^2\)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m First, expand both squares:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 101^2 = (100 + 1)^2 = 100^2 + 2 \cdot 100 \cdot 1 + 1^2
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 99^2 = (100 - 1)^2 = 100^2 - 2 \cdot 100 \cdot 1 + 1^2
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Now, subtract \(99^2\) from \(101^2\):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 101^2 - 99^2 = (100^2 + 2 \cdot 100 \cdot 1 + 1^2) - (100^2 - 2 \cdot 100 \cdot 1 + 1^2)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Simplify the expression by combining like terms:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 101^2 - 99^2 = 100^2 + 2 \cdot 100 \cdot 1 + 1^2 - 100^2 + 2 \cdot 100 \cdot 1 - 1
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m = 100^2 + 2 \cdot 100 \cdot 1 + 1^2 - 100^2 + 2 \cdot 100 \cdot 1 - 1
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m = 2 \cdot 100 \cdot 1 + 1 - 100^2 + 2 \cdot 100 \cdot 1
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m = 200 + 1 - 100^2 + 2 \cdot 100
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m = 201 - 100^2 + 200
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Instead of combining terms and then taking the difference, we can also calculate the squares directly using formula:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \text{Difference} = |a^2 - b^2|
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Here \(a = 100\) and \(b = 99\)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 101^2 - 99^2 = | (100)^2 - (99)^2|
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m By expanding squares:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 100^2 = 10000
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 99^2 = 9801
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Therefore,
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 101^2 - 99^2 = |10000 - 9801| = |199|
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 101^2 - 99^2 = 199
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So the absolute value of the difference of squares between 101 and 99 is:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \boxed{199}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 	endif
