[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m In Pascal's Triangle, each number is the sum of the number just above it and to the left and the number just above it and to the right. So the middle number in Row 2 is $2$ because $1+1=2.$ What is the sum of the numbers in Row 8 of Pascal's Triangle?
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{tabular}{rccccccccccc}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Row 0:& & & & & & 1\\\noalign{\smallskip\smallskip}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Row 1:& & & & & 1 & & 1\\\noalign{\smallskip\smallskip}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Row 2:& & & & 1 & & 2 & & 1\\\noalign{\smallskip\smallskip}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Row 3:& & & 1 & & 3 & & 3 & & 1\\\noalign{\smallskip\smallskip}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Row 4:& & 1 & & 4 & & 6 & & 4 & & 1\\\noalign{\smallskip\smallskip}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Row 5:& 1 & & 5 & & 10 & & 10 & & 5 & & 1\\\noalign{\smallskip\smallskip}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \end{tabular}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the sum of the numbers in Row 8 of Pascal's Triangle, we need to calculate the sum of 1 through 8.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$\left(\sum_{k=0}^{8} \binom{8}{k}\right)$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m We can use Binomial Expression rules to break this down.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m First, recall the Binomial Expression rule for $$(a + b)^n \):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$d_u(a+b)^n = a + b$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Using this, we can derive:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$\sum_{k=0}^{8} \binom{8}{k} = \binom{8}{0}d_o(8) + \binom{8}{1}d_o(9) + \binom{8}{2}d_1(10)$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$8! = 1 \cdot 8 \cdot 7 \cdot 6 \cdot 5 \cdot 4 \cdot 3 \cdot 2 \cdot 1$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$8! \cdot \binom{8}{0}d_0(0) + \binom{8}{1}(a) \cdot \binom{8}{1}(b)$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$8! \cdot \binom{8}{0}+8! \cdot \binom{8}{1}$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$s_0 + s_1$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Where $s_0$ is the sum of the three basic results of the Binomial Expression rule on d_0 and d_1, and $s_1$ is the sum of the first 8 uppercase binomial coefficients.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Since d_0 = 1, d_1 = 9. To find $s_0$, we should have the correct result for $a + b$. By the property (number in left hand side * number in right hand side)^2 is $binom{8}{0}binom{8}{0}$. By substitution: $a = b = d_o$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{align}\binom{8}{0}d_0^2 &= 1 \cdot 1\end{align}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$s_0 = 1048576$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Since $s_0 = sum_n\binom{8}{n} = 64$, the sum of the numbers in Row 8 Is $$\boxed{629084}.$$<|endoftext|>
