[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Given equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$ |n+6|=2-n $$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To solve for $n$, we need to consider the different cases for the absolute value. There are two possible cases:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Case 1: $n+6 = 2-n$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Here, we have an equation with a negative squared term (+6 and -2). We can solve for $n$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$n + 6 = 2 - n$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$2n = 2 - 6$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$n = \frac{2 - 6}{2}$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$n = \frac{2}{2} - \frac{6}{2}$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$n = 1 - 3$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$n = -2$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Case 2: $n+6 = -(2-n)$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m We can solve for $n$ in this equation by isolating the absolute value:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$n+6 = -2+n$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$n + 6 = -2 - n$$ + $n$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Collecting like terms and solving for $n$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$n + n - 6 = -2$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$2n - 6 = -2$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$2n = -2 + 6$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$2n = 4$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$n = 2$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So, we have found two solutions for $n$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$n = -2 \quad \text{and} \quad n = 2$$
