[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The cotangent of an angle is defined as \ \begin{align} \cot \theta =& \frac{1}{\tan \theta} \ \end{align} since \ \begin{align} \tan \theta =& \frac{\sin \theta}{\cos \theta} \ \end{align} Therefore, \begin{align} \cot \frac{3 \pi}{2} =& 1 \ \text{if} \ \sin \frac{3 \pi}{2} = \cos \frac{3 \pi}{2}. \end{align} We know that \ \begin{align} \sin \theta =& \pm 1 \ \text{if} \ \pi < \theta < 2 \pi \ \end{align} So, \begin{align} \cos \frac{3 \pi}{2} =& \pm 1 \ \text{and} \ \pi < \frac{3 \pi}{2} < 2 \pi \ \end{align} Since \ \sqrt{3} \ \text{is irrational, it doesn't exist as a real number.} \end{align}
