[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $\text{ADX^2} + \text{AEB^2} = \text{AEB^2}$, so we must solve for $\text{ADX}$. If we eliminate right triangles, $\text{ADB}$ and $\text{ADE}$, then $ABEC$ is a $45^\circ+45^\circ$ and $90^\circ$ triangle. In this triangle, $S_{\text{angles}} = 45^\circ + 45^\circ + 90^\circ$, which is $180^\circ$. Compute all angles and the surrounding triangles, as shown in the figure. In the $180^\circ$ $\text{orange angle}$ triangle $\text{ABE}$, apply the Law of Cosines to $\text{summed initial coordinates}$ \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ 3 & 4 \end{bmatrix}  – \sqrt{3}. \quad \boxed{6} $. Compute all other surrounding triangles and angles as shown in the figure. Apply the Law of Cosines to the remaining triangle. In this triangle, apply the Law of Cosines to $\text{summed initial coordinates}$ \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 \\ 2 & 2 \end{bmatrix}  – \sqrt{3}. \quad \boxed{7} $. Compute the final answer.
