[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The output from the symbolic solver indicates two pairs of potential solutions:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m - One solution is extremely complex and not applicable: `-2 * sqrt(2) / 5 - sqrt(2) / 5 - sqrt(sqrt(2) * sqrt(2 - 2*sqrt(2)) - sqrt(2)) / (sqrt(2) + 2)`
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m - The other solution is a complex one that evaluates to a non-trivial real number at some value:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m ### Proposed Solution:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m - Solution is:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m   [
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m   x = -2*sqrt(2)/5 - sqrt(2)/5 + sqrt(sqrt(2)*sqrt(2 - 2*sqrt(2)) - sqrt(2))/(sqrt(2) + 2)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m   ]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m ### Notice that even the complex solution 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m `sqrt(sqrt(2)*sqrt(2 - 2*sqrt(2)) - sqrt(2))/(sqrt(2) + 2)`
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m doesn't affect the essence of the equation because it implies the necessity of considering the non-real part only (without duplicates stacking) and carries a much larger complexity. Thus, the straightforward solution:
