[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To compute $\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 \\ 4 & 8 \\ \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$, we shall perform multi-step operations of matrix multiplication.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m We'll make use of the multiplication of matrices followed specifically to compute $\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} p \\ q \\ \end{pmatrix}$ as $\begin{pmatrix} ap + bq \\ cp + dq \\ \end{pmatrix}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Using the rule for finding the product of a matrix and a vector, we have
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$\begin{align} & \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 \\ 4 & 8 \\ \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} \\ = & \begin{pmatrix} (1)(5) + (2)(3) \\ (4)(5) + (8)(3) \end{pmatrix} \\ = & \begin{pmatrix} 11 \\ 32 \end{pmatrix} \end{align}$$
