[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m A palindrome is a number that reads the same forwards and backwards, such as 3003. How many positive four-digit integers are palindromes?
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m If the first and third digits are the same, there are 2 of those numbers.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m If the first and second digits are the same, there are 25 of those numbers.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m If the second and third digits are the same, there are 25 of those numbers.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m If the third and fourth digits are the same, there are 25 of those numbers.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m If all four digits are the same, there are 25 of those numbers.
