[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Sure thing! To solve this problem, we need to understand the minimum sum we can achieve from rolling two die with the digits $1$ through $8$. 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m First, let’s break down the idea of rolling two such octahedral dice.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m A normal pair of dice has a sum of $1 + 2 = 3$ to $7 + 6 = 13$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Therefore, when we roll two dice, and consider charging on different outcomes, our possible totals range.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m That means there are many possible sums when two dice is rolled. But among those sums, we should narrow down possible values, starting from minimal and progressing as we have keys '1-8' to extend through possible sums $27$ here.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Now accepting these, all possible sums from both dice 1-8 forms when rolling two dice:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$ 1 + 1 = 2, 1 + 2 = 3, 1 + 3 = 4, 1 + 4 = 5, 1 + 5 = 6, 1 + 6 = 7, 1 + 7 = 8, 1 + 8 = 9, 2 + 2 = 4, 2 + 3 = 5, ~~\cdots, 8 + 8 = 18$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m All sums from '2' to '18' should range based on how rolling these two dice could sum up: from $2$ to $72$ when rolling two octahedral dice. Now, to obtain 15: There could be multiple scenarios:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m - When the dice complement sum to exactly 15. This means rolling two dice, one of the numbers $2-8=1$ directly. One possible scenario: $(1, -1)$, which added up to $2$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m - When the dice sum to $8$ (only one way): Both dice add to $8$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m - When the dice sum to $7$ (2 out of 4) which gives another way: $(1, -1)$. Individually, both dice add to sum of $7$ but I can ‘put the two together, this is even the same sum itself.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So overall we have to figure out: How many ways there are to sum to exactly '15', and when different combinations
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Thus, we will calculate the number of combination "approaching 15" satisfactorily and it's weighing: any way of fitting sum to 15 results to each Combination of rolls. But check in the possibilities for both dice:\begin{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m | \calc[i=1,8 - i]{0,15} &=3, \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m | \calc[i=1,8 - i]{+i,15} &= 3, \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m | \calc[i=1,8 - i]{15-2i} = 1.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \end{aligned} So naturally the 15 could be in two outcomes with only difference in digit (either will be the answer.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{aligned}
