[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The roots of
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[z^7 = -\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} - \frac{i}{\sqrt{2}}\]are $\text{cis } \theta_1$, $\text{cis } \theta_2$, $\dots$, $\text{cis } \theta_7$, where $0^\circ \le \theta_k < 360^\circ$ for all $1 \le k \le 7$.  Find $\theta_1 + \theta_2 + \dots + \theta_7$.  Give your answer in degrees.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Here is the full answer.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m We are given that \[z^7 = -\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} - \frac{i}{\sqrt{2}} = \text{cis } 60^\circ - \text{cis } 120^\circ.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m This means that the roots of the equation can be written as \[\text{cis } \theta_1 = \text{cis } 60^\circ = \frac{1}{2} + \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}i\ \text{and} \ \text{cis } \theta_2 = \text{cis } 120^\circ = \frac{1}{2} - \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}i.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The sum of the angles for these roots is $60^\circ + 120^\circ = 180^\circ$, so the sum of the angles is $7 \times 180^\circ = 1260^\circ$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So, the answer is $\boxed{1260^\circ}$.<|endoftext|>
