[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2. Next, we can use the pythagorean theorem to find the length of the base of the parallelogram. Since the height of the parallelogram is perpendicular to the base, we can establish a right triangle where the height is one leg, the base and the hypotenuse are the other two sides.
