[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m We can use Vieta's formulas, which relate the coefficients of a polynomial to sums and products of its roots. For a quadratic equation \(ax^2 + bx + c \geq 0\):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m x + y = -\frac{b}{a}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m xy = \frac{c}{a}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m In our equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
