[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m  italian will just be checking if the point $(a, b)$ reflected over the $y$-axis indeed has a corresponding point that will visually match with $(j, k)$. This will necesarily involves the symmetry of the $y$-axis, which swaps the $x$-coordinate (i.e., $-x$) to the $-y$-coordinate (i.e., $-y$).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Given that $(a, b)$ is a general point on a Cartesian plane, we can find the reflected point $(j, k)$ by replacing $x$ and $y$ in the original point with their respective signs (-):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1. The reflection of a point $(x, y)$ over the $y$-axis results in the reflected point $(-x, y)$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2. Given the condition $a + j = 0$, we have $j = -a$. So, the reflected point $(j, k)$ is $(-a, k)$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 3. However, we also have $b + k = 0$. So, the reflected point $(j, k)$ should satisfy this condition, i.e., $k = -b$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m We now satisfy the symmetry of the $y$-axis as the second given condition. This leaves us with just one equation with two unknowns (i.e., $b$ and $k$):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1. $k = -b$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2. $a + j = 0$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 3. $b + k = 0$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Using these four equations, we can determine the values of $b$ and $k$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m  italian
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Italian is correct. The reflection point over the y-axis from $(a, b)$ will end up at $(-a, b)$. For the y-axis reflection—that is, the point over the y-axis—the transformed coordinate is $-ay$. Inserting $a$ for $x$ and $-ay$ for $y$ as the new coordinates yields the coordinates of the reflected point as $-a, b$, which approximately matches the given $a + j = 0$ since $-a$ represents $j$ ($-a$) and $b$ ($b$) when real numbers are involved. After performing the calculation, we find $b = -2$.
