[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the integer closest to the cube root of 100, we'll follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Step 1:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    - Calculate the cube root of 100.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    - Round the result to the nearest integer.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The cube root of 100 is approximately 4.641588824574032.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Step 2:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    - Compare the calculated result with the cube root of 100 rounded to the nearest integer.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    - Since 100 is closer to 99 than to 101, 4 is less than 4.641588824574032. Remaining fractional numbers in between remain as another possible integer, since they still lie within 7 decimal places.
