[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m I will assume:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The given vectors are orthogonal@en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orcs.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $\mathbf{a} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 1 \\ 3\end{pmatrix}$ and $\mathbf{b}$ are orthogonal@en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orcs.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $\mathbf{a} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 1 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m and we need to find $\mathbf{b} \in \mathbb{R}^4$ such that $\operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{b}} \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -\frac{3}{5} \\ -\frac{6}{5} \end{pmatrix}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Using the definition of ____projection, we set:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$\mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b} = \operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{b}} \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $\begin{align} 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \overrightarrow{a}_{\bullet} = \begin{pmatrix} x_1 \\ x_2 \\ x_3 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} a_1 \\ a_2 \\ a_3 \end{pmatrix} & = \begin{pmatrix} x_1 a_1 + x_2 a_2 + x_3 a_3 \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \Leftrightarrow \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m x_1 a_1 + x_2 a_2 - x_1^2 + x_3 x_3 = x_1 a_1 + x_2 a_2 + x_3 a_3 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \end{align}$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m All non-zero multiples \(x_i\) such that $x_1 x_2 + x_2 x_3 + x_3 x_1 = 0$ and $\overrightarrow{a}_{\bullet}$ is orthogonal to $\mathbf{a}$. In other words, all vectors $v$ among \(\mathbf{a}\) and $\mathbf{b}$ that are orthogonal to \(\mathbf{a}\) and forming an angle of $\pi$ form up orthogonal vector triple system. Performing a cross-multiplication of those vectors we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$a_1 x_2 + a_2 x_3 = 0$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$x_1 a_1 = 0$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Substituting \(a(x_1) = x_1\):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$a(x_2 + a_3) = 0$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The solution \(a \neq 0, a \neq 0\) or \(a = 0, a = 0\) is 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$a = \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -4 \\ -6 \end{pmatrix}, \mathbf{b} = \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 6 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The perpendicular vector triple system formed by them:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$\mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b} = -4$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find $\mathbf{b}$ we solve:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ 1 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} -3 \\ 6 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix} = -4$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$-16$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m For this we find the ordinary dot product:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$(2 \cdot -3) + (1 \cdot 6) + (3 \cdot -2) = -16$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Taking positive roots:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$x_1 = \frac{2 \cdot -3 + 1 \cdot 6 + 3 \cdot -2}{3 + 1} = \frac{10}{4} = \frac{5}{2}$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$x_2 = \frac{-3 \cdot -3 + 6 \cdot 6 + 2 \cdot -2}{3 + 1} = \frac{-3}{2}$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$x_3 = \frac{-3 \cdot -3 + 1 \cdot 6 + -2 \cdot -2}{3 + 1} = -5$$<|endoftext|>
