[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The function $f$ is defined on positive integers as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[f(n) = \left\{
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{array}{cl}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m n + 10 & \text{if $n < 10$}, \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m f(n - 5) & \text{if $n \ge 10$}.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \right.\]Find the maximum value of the function.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To determine the maximum value of the function $f(n)$, we need to analyze the definition of $f(n)$. According to the definition, for $n$ less than 10, $f(n) = n + 10$. For $n \ge 10$, the function is defined recursively as $f(n) = f(n - 5)$. This recursive definition means that the value of $f(n)$ depends on its previous value.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Let's break it down step by step:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1. For $n = 10$: $f(10) = 10 + 10 = 20$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2. For $n = 11$: Since $10 \le 11 < 11$ (because $10$ is still less than 10), $f(11) = f(11 - 5) = f(6)$. Since $6 \ge 10$, $f(6) = f(6 - 5) = f(1)$. Since $1 < 10$, $f(1) = 1 + 10 = 11$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 3. For $n = 12$: Since $11 \ge 12 > 12$, $f(12) = f(12 - 5) = f(7)$. Since $7 \ge 10$, $f(7) = f(7 - 5) = f(2)$. Since $2 \ge 10$, $f(2) = f(2 - 5) = f(-3)$. Since $-3 < 10$ (because $5$ is still less than 10), $f(-3) = f(-3 - 5) = f(-8)$. Since $-8 < 10$, $f(-8) = f(-8 - 5) = f(-13)$. Since $-13 < 10$, $f(-13) = f(-13 - 5) = f(-18)$. 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m By continuing this process, we see that $f(n) = n + 10$ for all positive integers $n$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 4. Therefore, the maximum value of the function $f(n)$ is $10 + 10 = 20$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The final answer is \(\boxed{20}\).<|endoftext|>
