[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Each vertex of this parallelogram has integer coordinates. The perimeter of this parallelogram is $p$ units, while the area is $a$ square units. What is the value of the sum $p + a$?
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m [asy]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m size(5cm,5cm);
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m draw((-2,0)--(11,0));
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m draw((0,-1)--(0,6));
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m draw((0,0)--(3,4)--(10,4)--(7,0)--cycle);
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m label("$(3,4)$",(3,4),NW);
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m label("$(7,0)$",(7,0),S);
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m [/asy]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m We know that the perimeter is the sum of the lengths of all sides, and we also know that the area is the product of the lengths of all sides divided by two. Let's denote the length of one side of the parallelogram as $l$. Then we can set up two equations: \begin{align*} 2l + 4 + l + 8 &= p \\ 2l + 4 + l + 10 &= a \end{align*} Combining the two equations, we get $2l + 14 = p + a$, and dividing both sides by 2, we obtain $l = \frac{p+4+8+10}{4} = \frac{p+22}{4}$. Therefore, the value of the sum $p + a$ is $\boxed{\frac{p+16}{2}}$.
