[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the smallest four-digit positive integer divisible by 47, we need to find the remainder when dividing by 47.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The smallest four-digit number is 1000.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the remainder, we can use the modulo operation (mod).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1000 % 47 = 40
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 40 is the remainder when 1000 is divided by 47.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the smallest four-digit positive integer divisible by 47, we can add 47 to 1000 until we find a multiple of 47.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1004 = 40 * 24.6 + (remainder 4) -> 1004 is divisible by 47.
