[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Solve for $x$: $\frac{3x - 1}{4x-4} = \frac23$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To solve for $x$ in the equation $\frac{3x - 1}{4x -4} = \frac23$, we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Step 1: Eliminate the denominator by cross-multiplying.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \frac{3x - 1}{4x - 4} &= \frac23 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 3(3x - 1) &= 2(4x - 4)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Step 2: Expand the equation.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 9x - 3 &= 8x - 8
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Step 3: Isolate $x$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m By moving $8x$ to the right side and subtracting $8$ from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 9x - 3 - 8x = 8x - 8 - 8x \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 7x - 3 = -8
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Then move $7x$ to the right side and add $3$ to both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m x - 3 = -8 + 3 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m x - 3 = -5 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \boxed{x = -5 + 3}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$<|endoftext|>
