[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Let the number of vertices be $a$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m According to the properties of a pyramid, we know that the sum of the exterior angles of each face equals $360^{\circ}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m In this case, each face is a triangle, and there are $\boxed{ 6 }$ faces.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Since the sum of the exterior angles of each face is $360^{\circ}$, we can conclude that the sum of the exterior angles of this pyramid is $6 \times 360^{\circ} = 2160^{\circ}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$\therefore \frac{1}{2}a(a-1) = 2160$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Solving this equation yields $a=6$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Therefore, the number of edges of this pyramid is $6 \times 2 = \boxed{{12}}$.<|endoftext|>
