[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To compute $\tan 240^\circ$, we first find the reference angle between 0° and 360°.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The reference angle can be determined by subtracting the angle's measure from 360°.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m In this case, we can find the reference angle as $360^\circ - 240^\circ = 120^\circ$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Given that the trigonometric function is periodic, we can flip the reference angle clockwise and subtract one or two full cycles.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m In this case, we can subtract two full cycles of 120° from the reference angle to get the equivalent angle in the second quadrant.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Therefore, $\tan 240^\circ = \dfrac{-\tan 120^\circ}{1} = -(-2.51134) = \boxed{2.51134}$.圾 Examiner User
