[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the product \(\left(\frac{3}{6}\right)\left(\frac{6}{9}\right)\left(\frac{9}{12}\right)\cdots\left(\frac{2001}{2004}\right)\), we can observe that each fraction in the product can be simplified. Each fraction repeats every four terms with the numerator equal to the reciprocal of the denominator. Let's write out the first few terms to identify the pattern:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \frac{3}{6} \times \frac{6}{9} \times \frac{9}{12} \times \frac{12}{15} \times \frac{15}{20} \times \frac{20}{21} \times \frac{21}{24} \times \frac{24}{27} \times \frac{27}{30} \times \frac{30}{33}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Each term can be simplified as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \frac{a_n}{(a_n)(a_{n+1})} = \frac{\frac{1}{2^{n-1}}}{\frac{1}{2^n}} = \frac{1}{2^{n-1}} \times 2^n = 1 \quad \text{for } n \text{ odd}, \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m and \( a_n = \frac{1}{2^{n-1}} \) is a repeating sequence every four values.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So, the product can be written as:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \left( \frac{1}{2} \right) \left( 2 \right) \left( 3 \right) \left( 4 \right) \left( \frac{1}{2} \right) \left( 2 \right) \left( 3 \right) \cdots \left( 489 \right)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m This is a telescoping product, where most terms cancel out:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \left( \frac{1}{2} \right) \left( 2 \right) \left( 3 \right) \left( 4 \right) \left( \frac{1}{2} \right) \left( 2 \right) \left( 3 \right) \left( 4 \right) \left( \frac{1}{2} \right) \left( 2 \right) \left( 3 \right) \cdots \left( 489 \right) \left( \frac{1}{2} \right) = (\frac{1}{2})^{490}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Since \( \frac{1}{2}^{490} = \frac{1}{2^{490}} \), the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \boxed{\frac{1}{1024}}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
