[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the remainder when $1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + \dots + 9 + 10$ is divided by $8$, we first need to determine the sum of the first 10 positive integers. 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The sum $S$ can be calculated using the formula for the sum of the first $n$ positive integers:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$S = \frac{n(n + 1)}{2}$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m In our case, $n = 10$. Plugging in and calculating the result will give us the sum. Let’s compute this.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m "?>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m hreader
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m OK. The sum of the first 10 positive integers is:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$S = \frac{10(10 + 1)}{2} = \frac{10 \times 11}{2} = 55$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Now, let's find the remainder when 55 is divided by 8. 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$55 \div 8 = 7 \text{ with a remainder of } 3$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So the remainder when 55 is divided by 8 is 3. 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Therefore, the remainder when the sum $1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + \dots + 9 + 10$ is divided by $8$ is 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$ \boxed{3} $$<|endoftext|>
