[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m This math problem consists to compute the natural logarithm of the logarithm of the logarithm of 256 with base 256.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[\log_{\log_{\log_2 256} 64} 256.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m First we compute any lower logarithms of 256 and then another alle of them.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The log on the base 256 wants the elongated logarithm with base 256 and that logarithm with base 256.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find this longer logarithm we raise 256 to every altitude to equalize the 256 through 256ing 256 with some other base.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Here is how we find the position where the log of 256 is equal to this ones.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[\log_{\log_{\log_2 256} 64} 256 = \log_{\log_{\log_2 256} 64} {\log_2 64 \over \log_2 256}\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m NOTE: \[\log_n m = \frac{\log_b n}{\log_b m}\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Here is a how we get the raising of the base 256 with 256ing this with some other base.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Stella403: Notice there are three different logarithms, but when raised to each other they equal one, so that, together they are an inverse.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[\log_2 64 = \frac{1}{\log_2 256} \Rightarrow \log_{256} 2 = \frac{1}{\log_2 64} = \frac{1}{2 \log_2 256}\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Because we have several frontal groups:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{align}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \log_{256} 64 &= \log_{256} {\log_{256} 64 \over \log_{256} 256} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m &= \log_{256} {\log_{256} 64 \over 2\log_2 256} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m &= \log_{256} {\log_{256} (64)} \log_2 256 -
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \log_{256} (2\log_2 256) \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m &= \left\lbrace \begin{array}{l}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m {\log_{256} 64 \over 2} \cdot 1 - {\log_2 256 \over 1} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m = 2\log_{256 256} 64 - \log_{256 256} 256 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m = 2\cdot 2 = 4 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \end{array}\right.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \end{align}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
