[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m An isosceles right triangle is removed from each corner of a square piece of paper, as shown, to create a rectangle. If $AB = 12$ units, what is the combined area of the four removed triangles, in square units? [asy]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m unitsize(5mm);
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m defaultpen(linewidth(.7pt)+fontsize(8pt));
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m pair A=(1,4), Ap=(0,3), B=(3,0), Bp=(4,1);
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m draw((0,0)--(0,4)--(4,4)--(4,0)--cycle);
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m draw(A--Ap--B--Bp--cycle,linetype("4 3"));
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m label("$A$",A,N);
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m label("$B$",B,S);
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m [/asy]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the combined area of the four removed triangles, we need to calculate the area of one triangle and then multiply it by 4.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1. **Determine the side length of the original square:**
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    - Since \(AB\) is the side length of the square and \(AB = 12\) units, the side length of the square is 12 units.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2. **Determine the distance from \(B\) to the removed side:**
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    - The distance from \(B\) to the removed side is the radius of the circle that is removed along the diagonal of the square.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    - This radius is the distance from \(B\) to the midpoint of the diameter of the square. Since \(A\) and \(B\) are the diagonals of the square, the diameter of the square is \(12 \times 2 = 24\) units.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    - The distance from \(B\) to the midpoint of the diameter is half of the diameter:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      \text{Radius} = \frac{24}{2} = 12 \text{ units}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 3. **Determine the height of the removed triangle:**
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    - The removed triangle is an isosceles right triangle with the legs equal to half the length of the side of the square.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    - The legs of the isosceles right triangle have a length of \(6\) units (since \(AB = 12\) and each leg of the right triangle is half of \(AB\)).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    - The area of this triangle is:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \times \text{base} \times \text{height} = \frac{1}{2} \times 6 \times 6 = 18 \text{ square units}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 4. **Determine the combined area of the four removed triangles:**
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    - Since there are 4 removed triangles, the combined area is:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      \text{Combined Area} = 4 \times 18 = 72 \text{ square units}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Thus, the combined area of the four removed triangles is \(\boxed{72}\) square units.<|endoftext|>
