[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Sure! Exponentiation is repeated multiplication, so $7$ is multiplied by every term raised to the power of $1$. Therefore, you can rewrite the expression as:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$7(3y + 2) = 7 \times 3y  + 7 \times 2$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$= 7[3y  + 2 + 2]$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$= 7[3y] + 7[2  + 2]$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$= 21y + 14$$<|endoftext|>
