[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Let $-2\sqrt{1 - 1/c} < a < 2\sqrt{1 - 1/c} $
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m By angle bisector theorem, $\tfrac{1}{a} = \tfrac{1}{b} + \tfrac{1}{c}$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m If we uniformly choose $b$ to be largest real value in bold group below, then $b$ also has to be obtuse to maintain continuity of arbitrary triangle. This is possible because the parameter range for $a$ exists in particular range for $c$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m This is because as we can work out that the in-attribute of the unit circle is mostly the angle instead of the length on the unit circle. Essentially this means that the degrees of the angle of $b$ have to be at most zero or around one and in that sense the same end up being in range of the angle bisector equation.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m And in details let's look at these two equations in the form:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{aligned} \sqrt{1 - 1/c} = \sqrt{ab} &=\lambda\\ \sqrt{a} + \sqrt{b} &=\mu \\ x^2 &= a^2 + b^2 \\ && b > c \geq a\\ \end{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Putting it together on the basis of the last equation we can simply Squeeze On Both Sides with the $x$-equation and extreme values will remain valid.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{aligned} a+\sqrt{ab}=c &&&\text{ ⑾}\\ b+\sqrt{a} b &= c &&&\text{ ⑯}\\ \begin{aligned} abc &= (a+\sqrt{ab})(b+\sqrt{a} b)=a^2 b + a \sqrt{ab} + b \sqrt{ab} + b^2 = a^2 b + (a+b)b^2\\ && bc= &&a^2 b + a \sqrt{abc} \\ abc&= &&a^2 b +a b\sqrt{abc} + b^2\sqrt{abc} \\&=a^2 b +ab \sqrt{abc} +b^2\sqrt{abc} \\ \end{aligned} \end{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $\text{(i)}$ And $a>0$ will impose conditions too, so we conclude that:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{aligned} b+\sqrt{ab} &= c &&&\text{ ⑾}\\ b+\sqrt{a} b &= c &&&\text{ ⑯}\\ && a+b+c>0 \\ &&\text{ Now from bracket $1<b<c$ conservatively put bounds to $2$} \\ && \begin{array}{lll} \sqrt{b} + c =2&&\text { ⑽}\\ \sqrt{a} + b &=2&&\text { ⑷} \end{array} \end{aligned}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
