[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      Simplify:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      2n + 1 = 30
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      Subtract 1 from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      2n = 29
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      Divide by 2:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      \[  
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      n = 14.5
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 5. **Re-evaluate the class size without fractional students:**
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    - As discussed earlier, \( n = 14.5 \) is not an integer.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    - Trying larger values for \( n \):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      - If \( n = 15 \):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m        \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m        15 + 13 = 28
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m        \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m        This is less than 30.
