[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Let \[f(x) = \left\{
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{array}{cl}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2x + 1 & \text{if } x \le 3, \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 8 - 4x & \text{if } x > 3.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \right.\]Find the sum of all values of $x$ such that $f(x) = 0.$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To solve for \( x \) such that \( f(x) = 0 \), we need to consider the two cases defined by \( f(x) \):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1. \( f(x) = 1 \)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2. \( f(x) = 8 - 4x \)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Let's work through each case separately.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m ### Case 1: \( f(x) = 1 \)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Since \( f(x) = 1 \) for \( x \le 3 \), we can set up the inequality:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ 1 \le 2x + 1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Solving for \( x \):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ 1 \le 2x + 1 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ 0 \le 2x \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ x \ge 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So, \( x \) must be greater than or equal to 0. Since \( f(x) \) is defined for \( x \le 3 \), \( x \) can be any number in this interval.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m ### Case 2: \( f(x) = 8 - 4x \)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Since \( f(x) = 8 - 4x \) for \( x > 3 \), we can set up the inequality:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ 8 - 4x = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Solving for \( x \):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ 8 - 4x = 0 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ 4x = 8 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ x = 2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m However, \( x = 2 \) is not greater than 3, so it does not satisfy \( f(x) = 8 - 4x \).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Thus, the only value of \( x \) that satisfies \( f(x) = 0 \) is \( x \ge 0 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the sum of all such \( x \), we note that \( x \ge 0 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The sum remains at 0 since over the entire range of \( [0, \infty) \).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Thus, the final answer remains:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \boxed{0}
