[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m We can find the area by integrating the distance from the $x$-axis with respect to $y$ from $-8$ to $8$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m We can find the area by evaluating this integral.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $\text{Area}=\int_{-8}^{8} \sqrt{(x-4)^2 + y^2} \, dy = \int_{-8}^{8} \sqrt{(x-4)^2 + 4^2} \, dy = 2\int_{-4}^{4} \sqrt{(x-4)^2 + 4^2} \, dy$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Let $h(x) = \sqrt{x^2 - 8x + 16}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Hence, we have $2\int_{-4}^{4} \sqrt{h(x)^2 + 16} \, dy = 2\int_{0}^{16} h(x)  \, dx = 2(16 - \sqrt{h^2(4)})$.<|endoftext|>
