[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m If $\cos \theta = \frac{1}{3},$ find $\cos 5 \theta.$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$\cos 5 \theta = 5 \sin^3 \theta - 10 \cos \theta \sin^2 \theta + 5 \cos \theta$$ \newline
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Let $\cos \theta = \frac{1}{3}$ $$\sin^3 \theta = \frac{1}{3} \sin \theta$$, \newline
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$-10 \cos \theta \sin^2 \theta = 10 \times \frac{1}{3} \times \frac{1}{3} \sin^3 \theta$$ \newline
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \hspace{.2in}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So, $\cos 5 \theta$ is:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m  $$\cos 5 \theta = 5 \times \frac{1}{3} \times \left(\sin \theta - \sqrt{\left(\frac{1}{3}\right)^2 + 9}\sin \theta \right) + 5 \times \frac{1}{3} \times \frac{1}{3} \times \frac{1}{2} \sin^3 \theta$$ \newline
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Which is:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$=\frac{5}{3}\sin \theta -\frac{1}{3}\sqrt{\frac{10}{9} + 9}\sin \theta +\frac{5}{9}\sin^3 \theta$$ \newline
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Which is :
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$=\frac{5}{3}\sin \theta-1.35\sin \theta+0.29\sin^3 \theta$$ \newline
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Or,
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$=\frac{4}{9}\sin^3 \theta - 31.4\sin \theta + 2.9\cos \theta$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Finally:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$=\frac{4}{9}\left(\frac{1}{81} \sin^3 \theta - 27 \sin \theta\right) - 1.35\theta -0.49\sin^4 \theta$$ \newline
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So, we have
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$=\frac{1}{243} \sin^3 \theta - 3.6 \sin^2 \theta +0.037 \sin^4 \theta$$ \newline
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m This is:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$\boxed{\frac{1}{243} \sin^3 \theta - 3.6 \sin^2 \theta +0.037 \sin^4 \theta = 0.0370247 \sin \theta -3.648\sin^3 \theta + 168\sin \theta + 34001.285004}$$<|endoftext|>
