[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Find $9^{-1} \pmod{100}$, as a residue modulo 100.  (Give an answer between 0 and 99, inclusive.)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m It's an arithmetic problem about modular equivalence.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m I'll find a correct value for $9^{-1}\mod{100}$ by working with various residue pairs modulo $100$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$9^{-1}\pmod{100} = 2 \pmod{100}$$, for whole numbers $0\leq x < 100$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m From $0<x<100$, we get
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$x=9^{-1}\frac{1}{10^1}+10^1\left( - 1\pmod{10}\right) = \frac{9^{1}}{10} - 1 \pmod{100}$$,
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$$(x+1)\left[9^{-1}+ \left(\frac{10}{9^1}\right) \right]=-1 \pmod{100}$$ and
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$$(x+1)\left[ 10^1 \left( - 1\right).\middlepinter \left(\sum _{k=0}^{0.1} (-1)^k k\right).10^0- 1\right]\pmod{100}=\frac{1}{5120}-1 \pmod{100}$$,
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m From this we can conclude
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $Nine {m}{i}{n}{e}{t}_{9}{\left(color{blue}{minus}\right)}^{-1}\overline+ msg[url]<img> 2 \pmod{100}\Leftarrow9^{-1}_{m}{m}{i}{n}{o}{u}{r}{e}{r} - 1$ We can break down the calculations using the remainders of various operations on 9:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1. Calculate the modular inverse $9^{-1} \mod 100$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$9^{-1} \mod 100 = 25$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m (9 divided by 7 gives a remainder of 2, and then we subtract the appropriate multiple of 100 to get the correct residue).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2. Calculate $9^{-1}(10^1)$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$9^{-1}(10^1) = 25 \times 10^1 = 250$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m _Removed 250_
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Now, compute $9^{-1}(10^1 \leftarrow \frac{1}{10})(-1 \mod 10) = -1 \mod 100$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$9^{-1}(10^1 \leftarrow \frac{1}{10})(-1 \mod 10^1) = -1 \mod 100$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Isolate the term that eliminates $(-1 \mod 100)$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$25 \mod 100$$: 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$25$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Hence, $9^{-1} \mod 100 = 25$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $\color{blue}{\boxed{25}}$ is the answer.<|endoftext|>
