[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Sure. First, calculate the height of the pyramid. We can use the Pythagorean theorem (hypotenuse^2 = sqrt(base^2 + height^2)) to find the height.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m baseSide = 20 ft
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m height = 27 ft
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m volume = (1/3) * (baseSide^2) * height
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m volume = (1/3) * (20^2) * 27
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m volume = 10800 cubic feet
