[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The probability of rain tomorrow is $\frac{1}{11}$.  What is the probability that it will not rain tomorrow?  Express your answer as a common fraction.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the probability that it will not rain tomorrow, we can subtract the probability of rain from 1:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \(1 - \frac{1}{11}\). To subtract these, we need a common denominator. The easiest way to do this is to use 11 as the denominator:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1 - \frac{1}{11} = \frac{11}{11} - \frac{1}{11} = \frac{11 \times 11 - 1 \times 11}{11 \times 11} = \frac{121 - 11}{11 \times 11} = \frac{110}{121}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So the probability that it will not rain tomorrow is \(\frac{110}{121}\).
