[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Find the minimum value of
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[x^2 + xy + y^2\]over all real numbers $x$ and $y.$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the minimum value of
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[f(x, y) = x^2 + xy + y^2,\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m we can find the partial derivatives of
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[f(x, y).\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Using
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[f_x = \frac{\partial f}{\partial x} = 2x + y,\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[f_y = \frac{\partial f}{\partial y} = x + 2y.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The partial derivatives are
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[f_x = 2x + y,\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[f_y = x + 2y.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the critical points, we set the partial derivatives to zero:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2x + y = 0, \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m x + 2y = 0.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Solving the system of equations, we find
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[x = -y.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Substituting this into the first equation, we get
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[0 = 2(-y) + y,\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m which gives
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[y = 0.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Then, substituting back into either equation, we find
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[x = 0.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Therefore, the only critical point is
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[\boxed{(0, 0)}.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Finally, to find the minimum value of $f(x, y)$ at this critical point, we substitute
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[x = 0\] and
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[y = 0.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m We get
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[f(0, 0) = 0^2 + 0 \cdot 0 + 0^2 = \boxed{0}.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]<|endoftext|>
