[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Given the figure, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$\triangle PQR \sim \triangle .QRS \text{   (SSS congruence)}$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$QR =  RS $$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$ ∴ \angle PQR = \angle RSQ$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m In $\triangle .QRS \equiv \triangle .QRS \text{  (SAS congruence)}$, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$QS = SR =  RS $$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$ \angle USART = 180^\circ (dry ratio) $$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Thus, $\angle .PQR = 50^\circ$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Since $PR =  RS$ and $QR \equiv QS$, $\triangle PQR$ is isosceles with angle $P = 70^\circ$.<|endoftext|>
