[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the minimum area of the triangle for given points, we can find the angles using the fact that the sum of angles in a triangle is $180^o$. 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Knowing that we have given vertices position, we can use this property and write it as a system. We can begin with the standard formulation:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m A &= 1/2 \cdot |l_1 l_2 \cdot A_1 A_2| \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m B &= 1/2 \cdot |l_2 l_3 \cdot A_2 A_3| \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m C &= 1/2 \cdot |l_3 l_1 \cdot A_3 A_1|
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Given that: $(1,7)$, $(13,16)$ and $(5,k)$, where $5$ is $k$. 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So, we can write:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m A &= 1/2 \cdot |\l l_2 l_3 | no 7} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m B &= 1/2 \cdot |\l l_3 k | no 16} \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m C &= 1/2 \cdot |\l l_1 k | no 1 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The minimum value of the area which involves $k$ only is:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$B + C = \frac{1}{2} \cdot \l \vert l_3k \vert + \l \vert l_1 k \vert $$ 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Finally we can write the resultant value, over the value of $k$ as shown as:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$\frac{k}{2}\l |\l \vert l_1 l_3 k \vert \r + \l \vert l_2 l_3 k\ r \r \vert } \vert k r \vert $$<|endoftext|>
