[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m What is $123_{10}$ when expressed in base $5$?
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To convert $123_{10}$ to base five, we can follow the steps below.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Step 1: Identify the rightmost digit in $123_{10}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The rightmost digit is $3$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Step 2: Create a new number by placing $3$ in front of the digit in step 5.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Thus, $3_{10}$ becomes $33_{5}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Step 3: Multiply $3_{10}$ by $5$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $3 \times 5 = 15$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Step 4: Convert the result of multiplying $15_{10}$ to base five.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The right most digit of $15_{10}$ is $5$, so $5$ is in the same position as $3(5)$ in base five.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m We round $5$ up to make it $6$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Thus, $3 \times 5 = 15_{10}$ becomes $165_{5}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Therefore, $123_{10}$ expressed in base five is $\boxed{165_{5}}$ accordingly.<|endoftext|>
