[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the number of square yards of carpet needed to cover the floor of the room, we first need to calculate the area of the room in square feet. 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The formula to calculate the area of a rectangle is:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Area = Length × Width
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m For the given room:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m - Length = 12 feet
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m - Width = 6 feet
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So,
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \text{Area of the room} = 12 \, \text{feet} \times 6 \, \text{feet} = 72 \, \text{square feet} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Next, we need to convert the area from square feet to square yards, since carpet strips typically measure in square yards.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1 yard = 3 feet, and there are 3.048 square feet in 1 square yard, or approximately 1.09363 square feet.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Therefore, to find the number of square yards of carpet needed, we divide the area in square feet by the area in square yards (or cubic yard):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \text{Area of carpet needed} = \frac{\text{Area of the room in square feet}}{\text{Area of the room in square yards}} = \frac{72 \, \text{square feet}}{3.048 \, \text{square feet per yard}} \approx 23.22 \, \text{square yards} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So, the number of square yards of carpet needed to cover the floor of the room is approximately 23.22. Through this calculation, we can estimate the amount of carpet required.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
