[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Initially she had $72$ ice cream cones so we can write it as $72$. At noon she made $\frac{2}{3}$ of this so she at noon has $\frac{2\times 72}{3} = 48$ ice cream cones. To be 2 ice cream, at the end of the day, we can write $72+48+\frac{2}{3}\times 48$. You can substitute the correct value to find the answer.\boxed{128}\ Congratulations<|endoftext|>
