[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m In a physical education class, students line up in four rows to do exercises. One particular class has over 30 students, with three rows having the same number of students and one row having one more student than the other three rows. What is the smallest possible class size for this physical education class?
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m We are given a right triangle with the sides as $d$, $h$, $p$ where $d$ and $h$ are the two legs of the triangle, and $p$ is the any other side. From here, we know the following from the given information:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $d+4+h=p$. Since $h=d$ and $d>0$ that means $p=d+4$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $q$ is equal to the unknown side length that starts in the interior of the right triangle.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Since we know that $\ell, dh, 2q$ form a right triangle, then
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $\ell^2 = d^2 + dh^2$, which means $q^2=d+4+dh-hd$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m This will make us to simplify $q^2$ to 9, which will make $q = 3$ as a possible side length. So $d+h+3 = p$.But that means $d+h-p<p$, and since $p>d$. We get $h=d-3$. My answer is $p=13$.
