[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The function $f(x)$ satisfies
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[f(x) + 2f(1 - x) = 3x^2\]for all real numbers $x.$  Find $f(3).$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Given equation $$f(x) + 2f(1 - x) = 3x^2,$$ substitute $1 - x$ for $x$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m f(x) + 2f(1 - x) &= 3x^2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2f(1 - x) + f(x) &= 3x^2 + 2(3x^2) \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m f(1 - x) + f(x) &= 3x^2 + 6x^2 \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m f(1 - x) + f(x) &= 9x^2.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Using the provided function $f(x)$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[f(3) + f(1 - 3) = 27\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[f(3) + f(-2) = 27\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Using the provided function $f(x)$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[f(3) + f(1 - 3 - 2) = 27\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[f(3) + f(-3) = 27\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Solving for $f(3)$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[f(3) + (1 - 3 + 27) = 27\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[f(3) + 25 = 27\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[f(3) + 25 = 27\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[f(3) = 2\]
