[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Compute $\dbinom{5}{3}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To compute $\binom{5}{3}$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1. Understand that $\binom{n}{k} = \frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}$ (where $n!$ denotes $n$ factorial, i.e., $(n-1)!$ for $n > 0$)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2. For $\binom{5}{3}$, calculate $5!$: $5! = 120$. Factorial of 3 is $3!$: $3! = 3 \cdot 2 \cdot 1 = 6$. Subtract the $3!$ from the $5!$, resulting in the above formula. Divide by the $3!$ the rest of the $3!$: $120 \div 6 = 20$. 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So, $\binom{5}{3} = 20$.
