[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m If the $y$-intercept of the parallel line $y=-4x-18$ is denoted by $p$, what is the $y$-intercept of the line $x=p-3$?
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please write a program to solve it
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m  Gebäider apropriado para o código abaixo: $+p$ To solve the problem, we need to find the value of \( p \) and then use it to determine the \( y \)-intercept of the line of the given equation \( x = p - 3 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m ### Step-by-Step Solution:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1. **Find the \( y \)-intercept \( p \) of the given line \( y = -4x - 18 \):**
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    - The line equation \( y = -4x - 18 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    - To find the \( y \)-intercept, set \( x = 0 \):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      y = -4(0) - 18 = -18
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    - So, the \( y \)-intercept \( p \) is \(-18\).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2. **Determine the \( y \)-intercept of the new line \( x = p - 3 \):**
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    - Substitute \( p \) into the equation \( x = p - 3 \):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      x = -18 - 3 = -21
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    - The \( y \)-intercept of the line \( x = -18 - 3 \) is \(-21\).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m ### Conclusion:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The \( y \)-intercept of the line \( x = p - 3 \) is \(\boxed{-21}\).<|endoftext|>
