[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m We are given that $CDE$ is a $45^\circ$-$45^\circ$-$90^\circ$ triangle with $CD = CE.$  Since $DE = CD + CE = 2CE,$ we have $\cos D = \frac{CD}{DE} = \frac{CE}{2CE} = \frac{1}{2}$ and $\sin D = \sqrt{1-\frac{1}{4}} = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}.$  Since $AB = BC$, $BE = BE,$ and triangle $ABE$ is an equilateral triangle, we have
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[AB = BE = BE \Rightarrow \angle EAB = 60^\circ.\]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Because $\triangle ACE$ and $\triangle ABE$ are both equilateral, and $\triangle BCE$ is an equilateral triangle, we see $AB \equiv BC \equiv BC.$  Thus, $\triangle ACE \sim ABCE.$  We have
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$\frac{AC}{AE} = \frac{CE}{EA} \Rightarrow \frac{AC}{BCE} = \frac{CE}{BE} \Rightarrow AC = \frac{1}{2}BE = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} BE = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} DB.$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m We also have $\triangle ABC \sim ABC.$  Using our previously derived ratios,
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$\frac{AB}{BC} = \frac{AC}{AB} \Rightarrow \frac{AC}{1} = \frac{\sqrt{3}/2 AB}{C/AC} \Rightarrow \frac{AC}{1} = \frac{\sqrt{3}/2 C}{1/2} \Rightarrow AC = \sqrt{3}C.$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m But we know $AC = DB,$ hence $DB = \sqrt{3}C.$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m This is accomplished $\测算$ our triangle by setting of the apparent triangle, we see $\triangle ABE \sim ABE.$  This means
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$\frac{AE}{AB} = \frac{BE}{BE} \Rightarrow \frac{AE}{AC} = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \Rightarrow \frac{AE}{1} = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \Rightarrow AE = \frac{1}{2} \sqrt{3}.$$<|endoftext|>
