[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find out how far the car can travel on 8 gallons of gas, we need to set up a proportion. 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The ratio between the distance (192 miles) and gallons (6) should be the same for both cases. 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So, we have.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \( \dfrac{192 \, \text{miles}}{6 \text{ gallons}} = \dfrac{x \, \text{miles}}{8 \text{ gallons}} \)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To solve for \( x \), we will cross-multiply and then solve for \( x \).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 192 \times 8=6 \times x
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1536=6x
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m x=\dfrac{1536}{6}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m x=256
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The car can travel 256 miles on 8 gallons of gas.
