[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Calculate the divergence of the vector field $\vec{F}(x, y, z) = f(x, y, z)\uvec{i} + g(x, y, z)\uvec{j} + h(x, y, z)\uvec{k}$, where $f(x, y, z) = \frac{1}{(x+y)^2}$, $g(x, y, z) = y+z$, and $h(x, y, z) = z$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To calculate the divergence of the vector field \(\vec{F}(x, y, z) = f(x, y, z)\uvec{i} + g(x, y, z)\uvec{j} + h(x, y, z)\uvec{k}\), we use the formula for the divergence of a vector field:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \text{div} \vec{F} = \frac{\partial f}{\partial x} + \frac{\partial g}{\partial y} + \frac{\partial h}{\partial z}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Given the components of the vector field:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m f(x, y, z) = \frac{1}{(x+y)^2}, \quad g(x, y, z) = y + z, \quad h(x, y, z) = z
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m We need to compute the partial derivatives of each component with respect to their respective variables.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1. Compute \(\frac{\partial f}{\partial x}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m f(x, y, z) = \frac{1}{(x+y)^2}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Using the chain rule, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \frac{\partial f}{\partial x} = \frac{\partial}{\partial x} \left( (x+y)^{-2} \right) = -2 (x+y)^{-3} \cdot \frac{\partial (x+y)}{\partial x} = -2 (x+y)^{-3} \cdot 1 = -\frac{2}{(x+y)^3}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2. Compute \(\frac{\partial g}{\partial y}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m g(x, y, z) = y + z
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \frac{\partial g}{\partial y} = \frac{\partial}{\partial y} (y + z) = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 3. Compute \(\frac{\partial h}{\partial z}\):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m h(x, y, z) = z
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \frac{\partial h}{\partial z} = \frac{\partial}{\partial z} (z) = 1
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Now, sum these partial derivatives to find the divergence:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \text{div} \vec{F} = \frac{\partial f}{\partial x} + \frac{\partial g}{\partial y} + \frac{\partial h}{\partial z} = -\frac{2}{(x+y)^3} + 1 + 1
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Simplify the expression:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \text{div} \vec{F} = 2 + \frac{1}{(x+y)^3}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Thus, the divergence of the vector field \(\vec{F}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \boxed{2 + \frac{1}{(x+y)^3}}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
