[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To rationalize the denominator of $\frac{3}{2\sqrt[3]{5}}$, we can multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $\sqrt[3]{5}$, the conjugate of the denominator. This will eliminate the cube root from both the numerator and the denominator.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So, the rearranged expression becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \frac{3}{2\sqrt[3]{5}} \cdot \frac{\sqrt[3]{5}}{\sqrt[3]{5}}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Multiplying the numerators:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 3 \cdot \sqrt[3]{5^2} \cdot \sqrt[3]{5}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m And finally, multiplying the denominators:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2 \cdot \sqrt[3]{5^3} \cdot \sqrt[3]{5}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m ### Step-by-Step Calculation:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1. **Combining the Numerators and Denominators**: 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \frac{3 \cdot \sqrt[3]{5^2} \cdot \sqrt[3]{5}}{2 \cdot \sqrt[3]{5^3} \cdot \sqrt[3]{5}}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2. **Simplifying the Expression:**
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \frac{3 \cdot \sqrt[3]{5^2} \cdot \sqrt[3]{5}}{2 \cdot 5 \cdot \left(\sqrt[3]{5}\right)^3}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 3. **Simplifying Further Presently:**
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \frac{3 \cdot \sqrt[3]{25} \cdot \sqrt[3]{5}}{10 \cdot 5}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    <sub> |
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    Applying the property $\left(a \cdot b \cdot c^3\right) = a \cdot \left(c^3\right)$,
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      we get: 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \frac{3 \cdot \sqrt[3]{25} \cdot \sqrt[3]{5}}{10 \cdot 5} = \frac{3 \cdot \sqrt[3]{25 \cdot 5} \cdot \sqrt[3]{5}}{10}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    </sub>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    <sub> |
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    $\sqrt[3]{5} \cdot \sqrt[3]{5} \cdot \sqrt[3]{5} = \sqrt[3]{5^3} \cdot \sqrt[3]{5} \cdot 1 = 5$,
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m      Hence,
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \frac{3 \cdot \sqrt[3]{25 \cdot 5} \cdot 5}{10} = \frac{3 \cdot 5 \cdot \sqrt[3]{25}}{10} = \frac{15 \cdot \sqrt[3]{25}}{10}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    </sub>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    <sub> |
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    Dividing both the numerator and the denominator by $\sqrt[3]{10}$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \frac{15}{10} \cdot \frac{\sqrt[3]{25}}{\sqrt[3]{10}} = \frac{3}{2} \cdot \sqrt[3]{25}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    </sub>
