[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m A wooden model of a square pyramid has a base edge of 12 cm and an altitude of 8 cm. A cut is made parallel to the base of the pyramid that separates it into two pieces: a smaller pyramid and a frustum. Each base edge of the smaller pyramid is 6 cm and its altitude is 4 cm. How many cubic centimeters are in the volume of the frustum?
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the volume of the frustum, we need to calculate the volume of the original pyramid and subtract the volume of the smaller pyramid from it.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Step 1: Calculate the volume of the original pyramid. The volume of a pyramid is given by the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Volume = (1/3) × Base Area × Height
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The base area can be calculated as the square of the edge size, and the height is the altitude (8 cm) in this case:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Base Area = 12 cm × 12 cm = 144 cm²
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Height = 8 cm
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Volume of the original pyramid = (1/3) × 144 cm² × 8 cm
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Volume of the original pyramid = 384 cubic cm (rounded to the nearest whole number)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Step 2: Calculate the volume of the smaller pyramid. The volume of a pyramid can also be calculated using the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Volume = (1/3) × (Base Area / 2) × Height
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Now, let's calculate the volume of the smaller pyramid:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Base Area = Base edge length^2 / 2
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Base Area = 12 cm × 12 cm / 2
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Base Area = 72 cm²
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Height = 8 cm
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Volume = (1/3) × 72 cm² × 4 cm
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Volume = 128 cubic cm (rounded to the nearest whole number)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Step 3: Calculate the volume of the frustum. Subtract the volume of the smaller pyramid from the volume of the original pyramid:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Volume of the frustum = Volume of the original pyramid - Volume of the smaller pyramid
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Volume of the frustum = 384 cubic cm - 128 cubic cm
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Volume of the frustum = 256 cubic cm
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
