[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m For how many positive integers $n$ less than or equal to 1000 is $$(\sin t+i\cos t)^n=\sin nt+i\cos nt$$true for all real $t$?
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m First, we have $$(\sin t+i\cos t)^n=(\sin t)^n+\left(\cos t\right)^n i \tag 1$$ and $$(\sin t+i\cos t)^n=\sin nt+\cos nt \tag 2$$ so when the $$(2)\ \ \color{red}{\checkmark}$$, the equivalent of $$(1)$$ is $$(\sin nt+\cos nt)^n= (\sin nt)^n+(\cos nt)^n i$$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Then we find $n$ root's of $$(\sin s+\cos t)^n=1,2,3,...,n \tag 3$$ on the upper inioneure $$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m sol=\sqrt{\begin{cases}1\end{cases}}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$(the max value on singiature place is about $1.748$)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Then we can count it. We saw $adtsum=57$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $\color{red}{\text{reworked equation}}$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$\sin nt \cos nt+\left(\cos nt+\sin nt\right)^n=-\cos nt \sin t \tag 1$$ and $$\cos nt \sin nt+\left(\cos nt+\sin nt\right)^n=+\sin nt \cos t \tag 2$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m For $n=1$, $(1) \to$ $0$ and $(2) \to +\infty$  
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Let's assume $n \geq 2,1<n<1000$. Then we have that $$(1)-(2) \to$$ $$2 n-\cos nt \sin nt=+\cos nt \sin t-+\sin nt \cos nt - \sin^2 t+\cos^2 t$$ $$\to  2 n=(\cos nt)^3-\sin^2 T \cos nt+(\sin nt)^2 \sin t$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m But obviously, if we take all set of roots $s, t \in \left[0 , 2 \pi \right]$ then the number is $57$. Q.E.D.<|endoftext|>
