[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>user
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m A rectangular garden 50 feet long and 10 feet wide is enclosed by a fence. To make the garden larger, while using the same fence, its shape is changed to a square. By how many square feet does this enlarge the garden?
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To determine the increase in square footage when changing from a rectangular garden with a length of 50 feet and a width of 10 feet to a square garden, we need to find out the area of both rectangles and squares, and then compare them.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1. Calculate the area of the rectangular garden:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \text{Area of rectangular garden} = \text{length} \times \text{width} = 50 \, \text{feet} \times 10 \, \text{feet} = 500 \, \text{square feet}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2. Calculate the area of the new square garden:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \text{New area of square garden} = \text{side of new square}^2 = \left(\frac{50}{2}\right)^2 = 25^2 = 625 \, \text{square feet}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    Since the side length of the square is half of the rectangle's length, the side length of the square garden is 50 feet.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 3. Compare the area of the new square garden to the area of the rectangular garden:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \text{Increase in square footage} = \text{New area of square garden} - \text{Area of rectangular garden} = 625 \, \text{square feet} - 500 \, \text{square feet} = 125 \, \text{square feet}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Thus, the garden increases in area by \(\boxed{125}\) square feet.<|endoftext|>
