[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m We know that in an equilateral triangle $O$ is the only center for rotation the triangle, and $z_1$ and $z_2$ are on the circle centered at the origin with positive radius, so the center form an equilateral triangle (for me it looks like a lens).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m There is a rotation that gives us I dual equations $\begin{cases} |z_2|^2-|z_1|^2=2z_1z_2 \\\\ |z_1|^2-|z_2|^2=2z_1z_2 \end{cases}$ Thus I get $\begin{cases} z_2=z_1e^{i\frac{\pi}{3}} \\\\ z_1=z_2e^{i\frac{7\pi}{3}}\end{cases}$
