[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To compute $\cos 180^\circ$, we'll use what we already know:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $\mathrm{cis}(180^\circ) = \cos (180^\circ) + i \sin(180^\circ) = -1 + 0i$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Since $\cos (180^\circ) = -1$, we can substitute that directly into the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $\cos 180^\circ = -1 + 0i = -1$
