[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m  Comey
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Using the identity for complex numbers, we have $(\cos 185^\circ + i \sin 185^\circ)^{54} = (\cos (185^\circ - 185^\circ) + i \sin (185^\circ - 185^\circ))^{54}$. This will simplify the given expression.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m  Comey
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Let $z = (\cos 185^\circ + i \sin 185^\circ).$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m  Comey
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m We know that $(\cos \alpha - \sin \alpha)^2 = \cos^2 \alpha + \sin^2 \alpha - 2 \sin \alpha \cos \alpha = 1 - 2 \sin \alpha \cos \alpha$,
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Since $\cos 185^\circ - \sin 185^\circ = -2 \sin 185^\circ(\cos 185^\circ - \sin 185^\circ)$,
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Rewrite $-2 \sin 185^\circ(\cos 185^\circ - \sin 185^\circ)$ as $2 \sin (185^\circ - \pi) - 2 \sin 185^\circ$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m  Comey
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Therefore, $(\cos 185^\circ + i \sin 185^\circ)^{54} = (\cos (185^\circ) + i \sin (185^\circ))^{54} = (\cos 185^\circ)^{54}$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m  Comey
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Since $(\cos \alpha)^{p} = (\cos \alpha)' \cdot (\cos \alpha)^{p-1}$, we have $(\cos 185^\circ)^{54} = -2 \sin 185^\circ(\cos 185^\circ - \sin 185^\circ)((185^\circ - \pi))^{54}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m  Comey
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Therefore, $(\cos 185^\circ + i \sin 185^\circ)^{54} = -2 \sin 185^\circ(-2 \sin 185^\circ)((-1)^{54})(185^\circ - \pi)$<|endoftext|>
