[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The solutions to \( z^4 = -16i \) can be expressed in the form \( z_1 = r_1 (\cos \theta_1 + i \sin \theta_1) \), where \( r_1 \) and \( \theta_1 \) are the solutions to the equation. Given that the solution with the smallest \( \theta \) is \( \theta_1 = -30^\circ \) and the two other solutions are symmetric about the real axis, we can determine \(\theta_2\) and \(\theta_3\) and \(\theta_4\).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find \(\theta_2\) and \(\theta_3\), we use the fact that the equation is symmetric around the real axis. This implies \(\theta_2 = \theta_3\). Therefore, we can write \(\theta_2\) and \(\theta_4\) as \(\theta_1 + \pi\), so \(\theta_2 = \theta_3 = -30^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m With \(\theta_1 = -30^\circ\), the complex number can be written as \( -i\cos 30^\circ + i\sin 30^\circ \). Using the values \(\cos 30^\circ = \frac{1}{2}\) and \(\sin 30^\circ = \frac{1}{2}\), we get \(-i \cdot \frac{1}{2} + i \cdot \frac{1}{2} = i \left( -\frac{1}{2} + \frac{1}{2} \right) = i \cdot 0 = 0\) as the real part of this complex number. Thus, \(\theta_1 + \theta_2 = \theta_1 + \pi = -30^\circ + \pi = -30^\circ + 180^\circ = 150^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Next, we consider the complex number \( e^{i \cdot (2 \cdot \pi \cdot 2.4) + \pi} \), where \( z = -2.4 - i \) and \( z^4 = i \). Notice that \( e^{i \cdot 20 \pi} \) is the same as \( e^{i \cdot pi} \), and \((e^{i \cdot 20 \pi})^2 = 1\) (since \( e^{i \cdot 2n\pi} = 1 \) for any integer \( n \) and \( (e^{i \cdot 2 \pi})^2 = 1 \)). Thus, \((z^4)^2 = 1^2 = 1\), so \( z^4 = 1 \), and \( z = 1 \) (the principal value of \( e^{i \cdot 2 \pi} \) is just \( 1 \)).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Therefore, \(\theta_1 = -30^\circ\), \(\theta_2 = \theta_3 = -30^\circ - 20^\circ = -50^\circ\), and \(\theta_4 = \theta_1 + 180^\circ = -30^\circ + 180^\circ = 150^\circ\).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The final answer is \(\boxed{150^\circ}\). It is significant to note that \(\theta_2\) and \(\theta_3\) are the same, as the question asks for \(\theta_1, \theta_2, \theta_3, \theta_4\).
