[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m where \(a\) and \(b\) are the components of the direction vector \(\begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \end{pmatrix}\).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Given the matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \mathbf{P} = \begin{pmatrix} \frac{1}{50} & \frac{7}{50} \\ \frac{7}{50} & \frac{49}{50} \end{pmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m we can compare it to the form of the projection matrix:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
