[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Let $\bold{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\bold{w} = \begin{pmatrix} 11 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}$.  Find the area of the parallelogram with vertices $\bold{0}$, $\bold{v}$, $\bold{w}$, and $\bold{v} + \bold{w}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the area of the parallelogram with vertices $\bold{0}$, $\bold{v}$, $\bold{w}$, and $\bold{v} + \bold{w}$, we can use the cross product of vectors $\bold{v}$ and $\bold{w}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Let's break down the steps:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1. Define vectors $\bold{v}$ and $\bold{w}$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    $\bold{v} = \begin{pmatrix} 5 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix}, \,\,\,\, \bold{w} = \begin{pmatrix} 11 \\ -2 \end{pmatrix}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2. Compute the cross product $\bold{v} \times \bold{w}$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \bold{v} \times \bold{w} = \begin{vmatrix} \mathbf{i} & \mathbf{j} & \mathbf{k} \\ 5 & -3 & 0 \\ 11 & -2 & 0 \end{vmatrix}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 3. Calculate the determinant:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \bold{v} \times \bold{w} = \mathbf{i}((-3)(0) - (0)(-2)) - \mathbf{j}((5)(0) - (0)(11)) + \mathbf{k}((5)(-2) - (-3)(11))
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 4. Simplify each component:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \bold{v} \times \bold{w} = \mathbf{i}(0) - \mathbf{j}(0) + \mathbf{k}(-10 - 33) = \mathbf{i}(0) - \mathbf{j}(0) + \mathbf{k}(-133) = \mathbf{i}(0) + \mathbf{j}(-\mathbf{k}) + \frac{\mathbf{k}}{1}(-133)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \bold{v} \times \bold{w} = \mathbf{i}(0) + \mathbf{j}(-133) + \mathbf{k}(-133) = \mathbf{i}(0) + \mathbf{j}(-133) + \mathbf{k}(-133)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Thus, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \bold{v} \times \bold{w} = 66\bold{v} + 133\bold{w}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Find the area of the parallelogram:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \text{Area} = \| \bold{v} \times \bold{w} \| = \| 66\bold{v} + 133\bold{w} \|
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Now, calculate $\| \bold{v} \times \bold{w} \|$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \| 66\bold{v} + 133\bold{w} \| = \sqrt{66^2 + 133^2} = \sqrt{4356 + 17689} = \sqrt{21045}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Thus, the area of the parallelogram is:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \boxed{\sqrt{21045}}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
