[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Let \[f(x) =
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 9x+4 &\text{if }x\text{ is an integer}, \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \lfloor{x}\rfloor+5 &\text{if }x\text{ is not an integer}.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]Find $f(\sqrt{29})$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find \( f(\sqrt{29}) \), we need to follow the definition of the function \( f \). According to the problem, the function \( f \) is defined as:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m f(x) =
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 9x+4 & \text{if } x \text{ is an integer}, \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \lfloor{x}\rfloor + 5 & \text{if } x \text{ is not an integer}.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Since \(\sqrt{29}\) is not an integer, we use the second part of the definition:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m f(\sqrt{29}) = \lfloor \sqrt{29} \rfloor + 5.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Next, we need to find \(\lfloor \sqrt{29} \rfloor\). The number \(\sqrt{29}\) is slightly greater than \(\sqrt{28}\), so \(\lfloor \sqrt{29} \rfloor\) is slightly less than 4. Specifically, \(\sqrt{28} \approx 5.29132\), and \(\lfloor \sqrt{28} \rfloor = 5\). Therefore:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \lfloor \sqrt{29} \rfloor = 5.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Substituting this back into the equation for \( f(\sqrt{29}) \):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m f(\sqrt{29}) = 5 + 5 = 10.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Thus, the final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \boxed{10}
