[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m A circular sheet of paper with radius of $6$ cm is cut into three congruent sectors. What is the height of the cone in centimeters that can be created by rolling one of the sections until the edges meet? Express your answer in simplest radical form.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Since the sector cuts the paper into three congruent sectors, each sector represents $\frac{1}{3}$ of the circle. The radius of each sector is $\frac{6}{2} = 3$ cm.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The slant height of the cone can be found by cutting the sector in half. The radius of the sector is the same as the slant height of the cone. The distance from the top edge of the conical section to the base of the cone is also the slant height.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The right triangle formed by the slant height, the radius of the circular base, and the height of the cone has a right angle. The hypotenuse of this right triangle is the slant height of the cone.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Using the Pythagorean Theorem, we can find the height of the cone to be:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $\sqrt{\left( 3 \right)^2 + \left( \text{ height of} \right)^2} = \boxed{5} cm$etaryfi<|endoftext|>
