[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The least common multiple of 8 and 15 is 120 as found using calculator:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m We'll first list multiples of 8 and 15: 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Multiples of 8: 8, 16, 24, 32, 40, 48, 56, 64, 72, 80, 88, 96, ...
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Multiples of 15: 15, 30, 45, 60, 75, ...
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m As we see, no multiples of 8 divide the multiples of 15.  Hence, 120 is the least number which 15 divides and thus 8 is a least common multiple.
