[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the tens digit of the sum $7! + 8! + 9! + \cdots + 2006!$, we need to compute the sum and then find the tens digit of the result.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1. Calculate the sums for one over “6” to one over “432”:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $7! = 5040, 8! = 40320, 9! = 362880, 10! = 3628800, \ldots, 18! = 10067893488}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2. Since $7!, 8!, 9!,\ldots,18!$ have six digits each and $19!$ has seven digits, we can see that $10! + 11! + 12! + \ldots + 2006!$ has twelve digits in total, as follows in tabular form:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{array}{c|cccccccccccccccc}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m  & 10! & 11! & 12! & \ldots & 19! & 10068 & 100681 & 100682 & 100683 & 100684 & 100685 & 100686 & 10060 & 100602 & 100605 & 100607 & 100611 & \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m & \vdots & \vdots & \vdots & \vdots & \vdots & 1 & 2 & 1 & 511 & 511& 511& 511& 689 & 689 & 689
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \text{Therefore, } 10! + 11! + 12! + \ldots + 2006! = \underbrace{102248 \cdots \underbrace{101139} \cdots}_{2 + 2 = 460 \text{ digits}}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 3. To find the tens digit, take the result modulo $10000 = 8 \times 125$, which makes $72 = 8 \times 90$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \text{Tens digit of } 102248 \cdots \underbrace{101139} \cdots 9999 = 1 + 2 + 2 + 6 + 2 = 15 = 1 \times 8 \times 125 + 3
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \text{Therefore, the tens digit is } 3 + 1 = \boxed{4}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
