[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    3x(x+1) + 7(x+1) = (x+1)(3x) + (x+1)(7)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 3. Now, we can see that both terms have a common factor \((x+1)\). We can factor this out from the entire expression:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    (x+1)(3x) + (x+1)(7) = (x+1)(3x + 7)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So, the factored form of the expression \(3x(x+1) + 7(x+1)\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \boxed{(x+1)(3x+7)}
