[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m When the diameter of a pizza increases by 2 inches, the area increases by $44\%$. What was the area, in square inches, of the original pizza? Express your answer in terms of $\pi$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Comment if someone can't understand
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m  Orleans, Louisiana, May 2016
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Let $x$ represents the radius of original pizza and a new pizza has diameter $x+2$. So $x=\sqrt{a}$, for some constant $a$. Notice that for radius $x$, area  grows by 44$\%$, so $1+(\sqrt{a})^2\cdot 44%=\sqrt{a}\rightarrow \sqrt{a}=\frac{a\sqrt{a}}{50}\rightarrow a=25$. Now area is $a \cdot \pi x^2=625\pi$. Hence, the area of the original pizza is $\boxed{3125\pi}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m  Orleans, Louisiana, May 2016.<|endoftext|>
