[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m What is the radius of the circle inscribed in triangle $ABC$ if $AB = 10,$ $AC = 17,$ and $BC = 21$? Express your answer as a decimal to the nearest tenth.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m This problem involves the relationship of the area inscribed in a triangle to the semi-perimeter. 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m An inscribed circle touches all three sides of a triangle, and its radius is the length of the tangent from each vertex to the opposite side. The semi-perimeter is half the sum of all three sides.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m   
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m First, we calculate the semi-perimeter of triangle $ABC$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $s = \frac{AB + AC + BC}{2} = \frac{10 + 17 + 21}{2} = \frac{48}{2} = 24$cm
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Next, we calculate the area of triangle $ABC$ using Heron's formula.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m We obtain the area $A = \sqrt{s(s - AB)(s - AC)(s - BC)} = \sqrt{24 \cdot (24 - 10) \cdot (24 - 17) \cdot (24 - 21)}$ $= \sqrt{24 \cdot 14 \cdot 7 \cdot 3} = \sqrt{4032} \approx 20.135735441166014$cm² 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m  
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Finally, the radius $r$ of the incircle is the area of the triangle divided by its semi-perimeter.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $r = \frac{A}{s} = \frac{20.135735441166014}{24} = \boxed{0.84}cm$ 
