[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Let $z = e^{2i \theta}$, this has re $\operatorname{\rm Re}(z) = 2 e^{i \theta}$ and purely-imaginary $\operatorname{\rm Im}(z) = e^{i 2 \theta}.$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Given that $\tan \theta = \frac{\operatorname{\rm Im}(z)}{\operatorname{\rm Re}(z)} = 2$ so we're told to know this information and $e^{i 2 \theta} = \cos (2 \theta) + i \sin (2 \theta),$ cubed, to isolate $\sin (2 \theta)$ and give us $\cos 4 \theta.$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Wei $\sin^2 (2 \theta) + \cos^2 (2 \theta) = 1,$ thus $\sin(2 \theta) = - \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}},$ so this, powers up to first power of $\theta,$
