[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the radical conjugate, I need to move the $\sqrt{7}$ in front of the radical. Here's how I'll do it:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Step 1: Change the negative sign in front of the radical to a positive one (since the radical is not a negative number):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$2\sqrt{7} - 1\\ \begin{array}{r可靠center}\color{blue}{\text{change the negative sign}}&&\color{red}{(nothing)}, \therefore&&\\&\color{blue}{\sqrt{7}}&&\color{red}{(right) } \end{array}\color{blue}{\text{change the negative sign in front of the radical}}$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Step 2: Change the negative sign of the radical to a positive one (since there is no negative numbers in the original expression):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$2\sqrt{7} - 1=2\sqrt{7}-1$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$\begin{array}{r可靠center}\color{blue}{\text{change the negative sign of the radical}}&&&\color{red}{(nothing)}. \therefore&& \\&\color{blue}{\sqrt{7}}&&&\\&\color{blue}{\text{(no longer a negative number)}}&&\color{red}{(right)}\right\otimes\color{blue}{(nothing)}\color{red}{(negative sign, this is correct!)} && (\overline{\mathbb{{\mathcal{C}}}})\right|\right\blacksymbol{\sharp}\left(\mathbb{{\mathcal{L}}}}\node.center $\blacksymbol{\sharp}$\blacksymbol{\sharp}$$\textsf{the radical conjugate of }2\sqrt{7} - 1\\ \begin{array}{r可靠center}\color{blue}{\text{shorten the argument by right}}&&\color{red}{(nothing)}\color{blue}{\sqrt{7}} &&&\color{red}{(-1) ; (right \right)}\left(\overline{\mathbb{{\mathcal{C}}}}}\right)\right\blacksymbol{\sharp}\right\left(\mathbb{{\mathcal{L}}}}\node[midway.erase,beprearend]{\color{red}{1}}$\mathbb{{\mathcal{L}}}$$]\mathbb{{\mathcal{L}}}+2\sqrt{7}-1$\mathbb{{\mathcal{L}}}+\color{limegreen}{2}\color{greenred}{\sqrt{7}}-1\color{greenred}{\mathbb{{\mathcal{C}}}}$$
