[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To expand $$(x+3)(2x-4)(x-6)$$, we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1. Multiply first (x+3):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$(x+3)(x-6)$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2. Multiply the result by 2x:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$\left[(x+3)(x-6)\right](2x) = (2x^2-6x+3x-18) = (2x^2-y)$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 3. Multiply the result by 2
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$(2(2x^2-y)) = (4x^2-y)$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Finally, we take the difference of factors:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$4x^2-x$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Thus, the expanded form of $$(x+3)(2x-4)(x-6)$$ is:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$\boxed{4x^2-x}$$
