[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    -\frac{1}{\sqrt{12}} = -\frac{1}{\sqrt{12}} \times -12 = r^2
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    Simplified this greatly:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    r^2 = 144/4 = 12
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    hence, \( r = 12 \).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m     Adjusting for y-coordinate to t.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m     \[
