[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m A rectangular garden 50 feet long and 10 feet wide is enclosed by a fence. To make the garden larger, while using the same fence, its shape is changed to a square. By how many square feet does this enlarge the garden?
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To solve this problem, we first need to calculate the perimeter of the original rectangular garden:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \text{Perimeter of } \text{original garden} = 2 \times (\text{length} + \text{width}) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \text{Perimeter of } \text{original garden} = 2 \times (50 + 10) \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \text{Perimeter of } \text{original garden} = 2 \times 60 = 120 \text{ feet} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Next, let's assume the length of the garden in the new square shape is $x$ feet. Since the garden is enclosed by the same fence, the perimeter of the new square garden will be the same as that of the original rectangular garden. So, we can write the equation for the perimeter of the new square:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \text{Perimeter of square garden} = 4 \times x \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Since the perimeter of the square must be the same as the perimeter of the original garden, we can set these two equations equal to each other:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ 120 = 4x \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ x = \frac{120}{4} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ x = 30 \text{ feet} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Now that we have the length of the square garden ($x = 30$ feet), we can calculate the area of the new square garden:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \text{Area of new square garden} = \left(\text{length of new side}\right)^2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \text{Area of new square garden} = 30^2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ \text{Area of new square garden} = 900 \text{ square feet} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So, the new garden is 900 square feet larger in area.
