[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Find the greatest common factor of $144$ and $405$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the greatest common factor (GCF) of $144$ and $405$, we can use the prime factorization method:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1. Prime factorize the first number, $144$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    $$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    144 = 2 \times (2^4) \times 3
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    $$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2. Prime factorize the second number, $405$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    $$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    405 = 3 \times (3 \times 5^2)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    $$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 3. These factorizations are already in their prime factorized form, so no further prime factorization is necessary.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 4. The common prime factors are $3$ and $2$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    $$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    \operatorname{GCF}(144, 405) = 3 \times 2 = 6
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m    $$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Therefore, the greatest common factor of $144$ and $405$ is $\boxed{6}$.@NoArgsConstructor<|endoftext|>
