[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m When simplified, what is the value of $$(10^{0.5})(10^{0.3})(10^{0.2})(10^{0.1})(10^{0.9})?$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To simplify the expression, we can use the property of exponents $(a^x)(a^y)(a^z) = a^{x + y + z}$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The given expression is:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$(10^{0.5})(10^{0.3})(10^{0.2})(10^{0.1})(10^{0.9}).$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Using the property above, we can combine the exponents:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$10^{0.5 + 0.3 + 0.2 + 0.1 + 0.9}.$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Now calculate the sum:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$0.5 + 0.3 + 0.2 + 0.1 + 0.9 = 1.7.$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Thus:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$10^{1.7}.$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To combine the remaining numbers \(1, 7\), we just need to perform division:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$10^{1.7} = 10^{1 + 0.7} = 10^{0.7}.$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Finally, calculating \(10^{0.7}\) to a more familiar base:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $$10^{0.7} = 10\boldsymbol{\color{red}\cancel{10^{0.7}}}^{0.7} \boldsymbol{\color{red}\cancel{1}}^{0.7} \boldsymbol{\color{red}\cancel{10}}^{0.7} \boldsymbol{\cancel{\color{red}{10}}} = 11^{\boldsymbol{\color{red}\cancel{10}}}\boldsymbol{\color{red}{\phantom{\frac{1}{\left(11\right)}}}\phantom{\cancel{11}}} = 11^{\boldsymbol{\color{red}{\frac{1}{\left(11\right)}}}}.$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Subsequently, since the exponent \( \left(11\right) \) is positive and less than 1, the result, \(11^{ \frac{1}{^{(11)}}} \), essentially is equal to 11.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m However, since we're dealing with powers of 10 that are very close to the decimal point up to 11, we can infer the result to be very close to \(1\) since the precise decimal value of \(11^{ \frac{1}{^{(11)}}}\) aligns with the repeatedly repeating decimal form of that value, so it will round to 1.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Therefore, $$(10^{0.5})(10^{0.3})(10^{0.2})(10^{0.1})(10^{0.9}) = 11.$$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \boxed{11}<|endoftext|>
