[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So, the matrix is A = \left( {\begin{matrix} 4 & 1 \\ -9 & -2 \end{matrix}} \right).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m First, we compute $A^2$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m A^2 &= A \cdot A \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m &= \left( {\begin{matrix} 4 & 1 \\ -9 & -2 \end{matrix}} \right) \cdot \left( {\begin{matrix} 4 & 1 \\ -9 & -2 \end{matrix}} ) \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m &= \left( {\begin{matrix} 4 \cdot 4 + 1 \cdot (-9) & 4 \cdot 1 + 1 \cdot (-2) \\ -9 \cdot 4 + (-2) \cdot (-9) & -9 \cdot 1 + (-2) \cdot (-2) \end{matrix}} \right) \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m &= \left( {\begin{matrix} 14 & 2 \\ -36 & 5 \end{matrix}} \right).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Next, we compute $A^3$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m A^3 &= A^2 \cdot A \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m &= \left( {\begin{matrix} 14 & 2 \\ -36 & 5 \end{matrix}} \right) \cdot \left( {\begin{matrix} 4 & 1 \\ -9 & -2 \end{matrix}} ) \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m &= \left( {\begin{matrix} 14 \cdot 4 + 2 \cdot (-9) & 14 \cdot 1 + 2 \cdot (-2) \\ -36 \cdot 4 + 5 \cdot (-9) & -36 \cdot 1 + 5 \cdot (-2) \end{matrix}} \right) \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m &= \left( {\begin{matrix} 2 \cdot 4 + 1 \cdot 2 \\ -3 \cdot 4 + 5 \cdot 1 \end{matrix}} \right) \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m &= \left( {\begin{matrix} 8 & 2 \\ -12 & -8 \end{matrix}} \right).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Next, we compute $A^4$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m A^4 &= A^3 \cdot A \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m &= \left( {\begin{matrix} 8 & 2 \\ -12 & -8 \end{matrix}} \right) \cdot \left( {\begin{matrix} 4 & 1 \\ -9 & -2 \end{matrix}} ) \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m &= \left( {\begin{matrix} 8 \cdot 4 + 2 \cdot (-9) & 8 \cdot 1 + 2 \cdot (-2) \\ -12 \cdot 4 + (-8) \cdot (-9) & -12 \cdot 1 + (-8) \cdot (-2) \end{matrix}} \right) \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m &= \left( {\begin{matrix} 4 \cdot 4 + 6 & 4 \cdot 1 \\ -4 \cdot 4 + 9 & -4 \cdot 1 + 16 \end{matrix}} \right) \\
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m &= \left( {\begin{matrix} 20 \\ 5 \end{matrix}} \right).
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m From $A$ to $A^4$, the matrix is a cycle of length 2.  By the induction hypothesis, $\begin{pmatrix} 4 & 1 \\ 2 & 0 \end{pmatrix}^k = \begin{pmatrix} 4 & k+2 \\ 2 & 0 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\begin{pmatrix} 4 & k \\ -(7-k) & 0 \end{pmatrix}^k = \begin{pmatrix} 4 & 2k+3 \\ 7-2k & 0 \end{pmatrix}.$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To compute $A^{100},$ we multiply $A^{4k+1},$ $A^{4k+2},$ and $A^{4k+3}.$  But these give us matrices that reduce key rows and columns.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The key top-left entry is $\begin{pmatrix} 4 & k \\ 2 & 0 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 4+k+2 \\ 2^{9+2k} \end{pmatrix} = 4 \cdot 4 + 0 + 2^{k+6} = 16 + 2^{k+6}$, that is,
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \mathbf{A}^{100} &= 16 + 2^{100+6} = 1 + 2^{106},
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \end{align*}which is the same as $\boxed{\mathbf{A}^{110} = 2^{110+6} = 2^{116}}$.
