[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 1. Convert the base $9$ representations to base $10$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 2. Perform the addition in base $10$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 3. Convert the sum back to base $9$.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Let's start by converting each base $9$ number to base $10$:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m - $175_{9} = (1 \cdot 9^2) + (7 \cdot 9^1) + (5 \cdot 9^0) = 81 + 63 + 5 = 149_{10}$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m - $714_{9} = (7 \cdot 9^2) + (1 \cdot 9^1) + (4 \cdot 9^0) = 567 + 9 + 4 = 580_{10}$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m - $61_9 = (6 \cdot 9^0) = 6_{10}$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Next, we add these base $10$ numbers together. We know that the sum of base $9$ numbers follows certain rules, so we can directly add the remainders and use a calculator for more efficiency if necessary:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 149 + 580 + 6 = 735_{10}
