[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To solve this problem, we will first need to find the complement of the given angle. The complement of an angle adds up to 90 degrees. To do this, we will subtract the given angle from 90 degrees:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 90 - 42 = 48 degrees
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Now that we have the complement of the given angle, we can find the supplement of this angle. The supplement of an angle adds up to 180 degrees. To do this, we will subtract the complement from 180 degrees:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 180 - 48 = 132 degrees
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So, the degree measure of the supplement of the complement of a 42-degree angle is 132 degrees.rne
