[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The calculation is as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 987670 \mod 128
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Now, let's perform the division and find the remainder:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 987,670 \div 128 \approx 76,773.7187
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The integer part of the quotient, 76, is the remainder. To confirm, we can multiply the quotient by 128 and add the remainder:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 76 \times 128 = 987,36
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \text{Add the remainder: } 987,36 + 76 = 988,12
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Since we obtained a whole number, it indicates that the exact remainder should be the integer result of the division less than the divisor. Given that 988,12 is between 987,670 and 987,718, the remainder should not be less than 128.
