[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Tara rolls three standard dice once.  What is the probability that the sum of the numbers rolled will be three or more?  Express your answer as a percent.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the probability that the sum of the numbers rolled will be three or more, we first need to understand the range of possible sums from rolling three standard dice. Standard dice have numbers from 1 to 6. There's a perfect 6-sided die (number 1-6) and a 12-sided die (number 1-12). Therefore, we are considering sums up to 12-1 (not including 6) for each die.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m There are 11 possible outcomes for each die (11 total numbers, but only 6 faces on a single side). Let's calculate the total number of possible outcomes from three such dice:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 11 \, \text{outcomes/die} \times 11 \, \text{outcomes/die} \times 11 \, \text{outcomes/die} = 11^3 = 1331
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The total number of possible outcomes where the sum is 3 or more can be calculated by summing up the numerator:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \text{Total number of outcomes} = 6 \times 11 \times 11 + 1 - 6 = 660 \quad (\text{since there's one extra way for the sum to be 3})
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The total number of possible outcomes where the sum is 3 or more can be calculated as:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \text{Total number of outcomes} = \binom{3}{3} \times 11^3 + 1 - 6 = 11^3 + 1 - 6 = 1331 + 1 - 6 = 1330
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The probability that the sum of the numbers rolled will be 3 or more is then calculated as:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \frac{1330}{1331}
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find the value of this probability as a percent, we use the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \frac{1330}{1331} \times 100\%
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Calculating this gives:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 100\% \times (1330 / 1331) = 1330\%
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So the probability that the sum will be 3 or more when three standard dice are rolled once is \boxed{1330}.<|endoftext|>
