[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The angle measures of the three angles of a triangle are in the ratio $1:3:6$. What is the number of degrees in the measure of the largest angle?
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m There are three possible directions for finding the largest angle in a triangle with two three angle equal to one, leaving the sixth one free to determine:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Text book:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m The statements are incomplete as stated in a text book. Some of the angle angles can be 54 degrees, 72 degrees, or 108 degrees. In the following, we give the own complete solution to the problem:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m First, we write down the angles as fractions of 180 degrees:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $\dfrac{\mbox{To an angle }1}{3}=\dfrac{\mbox{To an angle }1}{3(3)}=\mbox{A flaw - pressure}=\dfrac{180-72\ \degrees}{3}=\dfrac{108\ \degrees}{3}\approx36 \Marshes}$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $\dfrac{\mbox{To an angle }2}{3}=\dfrac{\mbox{To an angle }2}{3(3)}=\mbox{Banana}=\frac{108\ \degrees}{3}\approx36$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $\dfrac{\mbox{To an angle }3}{6}=36\ \degrees$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m $\dfrac{\mbox{To an angle }1}{3}=36\ \degrees$
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Now, take into consideration all angles: the total is 360 degrees.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m This gives an outside angle of $360-180-180$, just like the one, and so the other three angles have never been written, leaving us with 360-360=0 degrees.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Cheers
