[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m At the beginning of my bike ride I feel good, so I can travel   20 miles per hour.  Later, I get tired and travel only 12 miles  per hour.  If I travel a total of 122 miles in a total time of   8 hours, for how many hours did I feel good?  Express your  answer as a common fraction.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m To find out how many hours you were feeling good at the beginning and how long you were feeling good afterward, we can set up a system of equations based on the information given.
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Let:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m - \(t\) = minutes (transformation time)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m - \(h\) = hours (total time)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m - \(m\) = miles (total distance)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Given:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m - \(m = 122\) miles
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m - \(8\) hours = \(8 \times 60 = 480\) minutes
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m - \(t \ge 0\), \(h \ge 0\), and \(t + h = 480\)
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m Our objective is to find \(t = t_1\) minutes when the distance is 122 miles. Substituting in, the given equations become:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ 122 = 480 - m \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ 8t = 480 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m From the second equation, we can solve for \(t\):
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ t = \frac{480}{8} = 60 \text{ minutes} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m We are given that at the first rate \(t_1\) minutes, the distance was 81 miles. Substituting this into the first equation gives:
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ 81 = 480 - 122 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ 81 - 112 = 111 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ t_1 + 60 = 72 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ t_1 = 72 - 60 \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m \[ t_1 = 12 \text{ minutes} \]
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=2119687)[0m So, the first rate \(t_1\) is 60 minutes and the second rate \(t\) is 120 minutes. Therefore, you were feeling good for \(\boxed{60}\) minutes at the beginning and \(\boxed{120}\) minutes afterward.<|endoftext|>
